  "method": "1. Scrub the potato, prick it a few times with a fork and microwave it 5 to 8 minutes, turning once, or bake it at 400F, 45 to 60 minutes, until a knife slides in with no resistance. Weigh the cooked flesh.\n2. Cut the cooked potato into small cubes and slice the red bell pepper into thin strips. Beat the eggs and egg whites with a pinch of salt.\n3. Heat the olive oil in a nonstick pan over medium, add the potato cubes in one layer with 1/2 tsp smoked paprika and a pinch of salt, and leave them alone, stirring only every couple of minutes, 6 to 8 minutes, until golden and crisp at the edges, because constant stirring stops the crust from forming.\n4. Add the pepper strips for the last 3 minutes, stirring now and then, until they soften and brighten.\n5. Push the potato and pepper to one side, lower the heat to medium-low and pour the eggs into the empty side. Let them sit 20 seconds, then fold them 2 to 3 minutes, until set with no runny parts (160F).\n6. Stir everything together, tip it into a bowl and top with the cheddar and salsa.",
