  "method": "1. If your grain is the white rice, rinse it, then simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice, about 18 minutes, and rest it 5 minutes off the heat. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice, 40 to 45 minutes, and rest it 10 minutes off the heat. If it is the quinoa, rinse it, which washes off its bitter coating, then simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, about 15 minutes, and rest it 5 minutes. If it is the riced cauliflower, cook it in a hot pan with a little oil, 4 to 5 minutes, stirring, until tender and dry. Weigh your grain cooked.\n2. If your protein is the chicken breast or chicken thigh, pat your protein dry, cut it into bite-size pieces, season with salt and pepper, and stir-fry it in your fat in a very hot wok or large skillet, leaving it 2 minutes to brown, then stirring 4 to 6 more minutes, until golden and no longer pink inside (165F).\n3. Add the broccoli to the pan with a splash of water, cover and steam 3 to 4 minutes, until bright green and crisp-tender, because the steam cooks it fast without drying it out.\n4. Stir in the teriyaki sauce, 1 tsp tamari, 1 tsp honey and the sriracha, let it bubble 30 to 60 seconds until glossy, then toss your protein and the broccoli in it.\n5. Spoon it over your grain and finish with a sprinkle of sesame seeds.",
