  "method": "1. If your grain is the white rice, rinse it, then simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice, about 18 minutes, and rest it 5 minutes off the heat. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice, 40 to 45 minutes, and rest it 10 minutes off the heat. If it is the quinoa, rinse it, which washes off its bitter coating, then simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, about 15 minutes, and rest it 5 minutes. If it is the riced cauliflower, cook it in a hot pan with a little oil, 4 to 5 minutes, stirring, until tender and dry. Weigh your grain cooked.\n2. Heat your fat in a large skillet over high heat until it shimmers, add the ground beef and leave it 2 minutes to brown, then cook 4 to 5 more minutes, breaking it into small crumbles, until no pink is left (160F).\n3. Add your vegetables and cook 2 to 3 minutes, until just softened but still with a little bite.\n4. Stir in the gochujang, 2 tsp tamari, 1 tsp honey and a splash of water, then simmer 2 minutes, until the sauce thickens and coats the beef, so it glazes the meat instead of pooling in the bowl.\n5. Spoon the beef over your grain and top with the kimchi, sliced scallion and a sprinkle of sesame seeds.",
