  "method": "1. Start your grain first. If it is white rice, simmer covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice, about 18 minutes, then rest 5 minutes. If it is brown rice, simmer covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice, 40 to 45 minutes, then rest 10 minutes. If it is quinoa, rinse well, then simmer covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, about 15 minutes, and rest 5 minutes. If it is the riced cauliflower, microwave it covered with a splash of water, 3 to 4 minutes, until hot. Weigh it cooked.\n2. Heat the oven to 400F, snap the woody ends off the asparagus, toss the spears with a little oil and a pinch of salt, and roast them on a sheet pan 10 to 12 minutes, until tender with browned tips.\n3. If it is the cooked salmon, pat it dry and season the flesh side, heat your fat in a skillet over medium-high until it shimmers, lay the fillet in skin side down and sear 4 to 5 minutes so the skin crisps, then flip it and cook 2 to 3 minutes more, until it flakes easily and reads 145F.\n4. If it is the canned salmon or the canned mackerel, tip the can into a sieve, drain it well, flake it into a bowl and toss it with your fat; there is nothing to cook.\n5. Squeeze lemon over your protein and add a little lemon zest and 1 tsp chopped dill, then serve it over your grain with the asparagus.",
