  "method": "1. Start your grain first. If it is white rice, simmer covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice, about 18 minutes, then rest 5 minutes. If it is brown rice, simmer covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice, 40 to 45 minutes, then rest 10 minutes. If it is quinoa, rinse well, then simmer covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, about 15 minutes, and rest 5 minutes. If it is the riced cauliflower, microwave it covered with a splash of water, 3 to 4 minutes, until hot. Weigh it cooked. Spread it on a plate to cool while you cook, so it fries instead of steaming.\n2. Heat your fat in a large pan over high heat. If it is the chicken, cut any whole chicken piece into bite-size bits and cook 5 to 7 minutes, until no pink remains (165F). If it is the eggs, beat them with a pinch of salt and scramble 1 to 2 minutes, until firm (160F). If it is the tofu, crumble it and cook 5 to 6 minutes, until golden. If it is the TVP, soak the TVP in an equal amount of hot water 5 to 10 minutes, squeeze it dry and cook 4 to 5 minutes, until browned. Move your protein to a plate.\n3. Add your grain to the empty pan, press it flat and leave it 3 to 4 minutes, until the bottom crisps. Chop the kimchi, fold it in with a splash of its juice and toss 2 to 3 minutes, until hot.\n4. Return your protein and toss 1 minute, then top with the hot sauce, a sprinkle of sesame seeds and sliced scallion.",
