  "method": "1. Dice your vegetables small, so the pieces soften fast and melt into the sauce.\n2. Heat the olive oil in a wide, shallow pan over medium and cook your vegetables 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until soft.\n3. Stir in 1 minced garlic clove, 1 tbsp tomato paste, 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp smoked paprika, a pinch of cayenne and a pinch of salt, and cook 30 seconds, because spices taste fuller after a short bloom in hot oil.\n4. Add a splash of water and simmer 8 to 10 minutes, stirring now and then, until the sauce is thick and jammy.\n5. Make little wells in the sauce with the back of a spoon, crack in the eggs and pour the egg whites around them.\n6. Cover the pan and cook over medium-low 5 to 8 minutes, until the whites are set and the yolks are no longer runny (160F).\n7. While the eggs cook, warm your carb in a toaster or dry pan, 1 to 2 minutes, until hot.\n8. Crumble the feta over the top, then serve from the pan with your carb alongside for scooping.",
