  "method": "1. Dice your vegetables small, so they soften in the few minutes the eggs take.\n2. Heat a little oil in a nonstick pan over medium and cook the vegetables 3 to 4 minutes, until soft.\n3. Add the black beans and warm them 2 to 3 minutes, mashing about a third with a spoon so the filling holds together in the tortilla.\n4. If your protein is eggs or egg whites, beat them with a pinch of salt, push the filling to one side, lower the heat to medium-low and stir them 2 to 3 minutes, until set with no runny parts (160F).\n5. Warm the tortilla in a dry pan, 20 to 30 seconds a side, so it folds without cracking.\n6. Fill it with the beans and eggs, top with your fat and the salsa, and roll it up tight, folding the sides in first.",
  "oil": "Use a light spray oil for the filling. For the optional crisped shell, use a thin film of avocado oil, its high ~520F smoke point handles the medium-high griddle sear without smoking or turning bitter. Skip EVOO or butter for that sear; they'd scorch at that heat. If avocado is on your list, keep it raw inside the burrito rather than frying it.",
