  "method": "1. Heat the oven to 375F.\n2. If your carb is the potato, cut it into 1/2-inch cubes, toss with a little oil, salt and pepper, and roast on a sheet pan 25 to 30 minutes, until golden at the edges and a fork slides in easily.\n3. In a small bowl, mix 1/2 tsp turmeric, 1 grated garlic clove, 1 tsp oregano, 1/2 tsp salt and black pepper.\n4. If your protein is the tofu, drain it and blend it smooth with a splash of water and the seasoning mix, until it pours like a thick batter, so the frittata sets without lumps.\n5. If your protein is the TVP, cover it with an equal amount of hot water, let it soak 5 to 10 minutes until soft, then blend it with the seasoning mix and a splash more water into a thick batter.\n6. Heat the olive oil in an oven-safe skillet over medium and cook your vegetables 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until soft and nearly dry, so the frittata does not turn watery.\n7. Pour the batter over the vegetables, smooth the top, and bake 20 to 25 minutes, until the top is set and the edges are golden.\n8. Let it rest 3 to 5 minutes, so it firms up and slices cleanly. If your carb is the whole wheat bread, toast it 2 to 3 minutes while it rests.\n9. Cut the frittata into wedges and serve with your carb and a spoon of the tzatziki.",
  "oil": "Olive oil (~375F) is ideal double-duty here: it sits right at its comfort zone for both the medium-heat stovetop saute and the 375F bake, and it adds Mediterranean flavor. Refined avocado oil works too if you want more headroom, but at this temperature olive oil is the better-tasting choice.",
