  "method": "1. Pat the shrimp bone-dry with paper towels, so they sear instead of steam, then season with 1 tsp chili powder, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp garlic powder and salt.\n2. Shred or slice your vegetables thin, so the pieces stay crunchy and fit in a taco.\n3. Heat a little oil in a skillet over medium-high until it shimmers, then cook the shrimp in one layer 2 to 3 minutes total, turning once, until pink, opaque and curled with a little char (145F). Add 2 minced garlic cloves for the last 30 seconds, and pull the shrimp the moment they are done, because they turn rubbery fast.\n4. Char your carb over a gas flame with tongs, or in a dry hot pan, 20 to 30 seconds a side, until it blisters.\n5. Pile the shrimp into the warm tortillas and top with your vegetables, the salsa, sliced avocado and a dash of the sriracha, plus a squeeze of lime.",
