  "method": "1. If your carb is the brown rice or the white rice, simmer your carb covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice, 40 to 45 minutes for brown or 16 to 18 minutes for white, then rest 5 minutes and weigh it cooked. If it is the quinoa, rinse it and simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup 15 minutes, then rest 5 minutes and weigh it cooked. If it is the riced cauliflower, cook it in a dry skillet 4 to 5 minutes, until tender. If it is the refried beans, warm them in a small pot with a splash of water 3 to 4 minutes, stirring, until loose and creamy.\n2. Season your protein with 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp chili powder, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp oregano, 1/2 tsp garlic powder and salt.\n3. If your protein is the chicken breast, cut it into bite-size pieces and sear it in a hot skillet with a little oil over medium-high, 6 to 8 minutes, stirring, until no pink remains and it reads 165F. If it is the chicken thigh, cut it into bite-size pieces and sear it in a hot skillet with a little oil over medium-high, 7 to 9 minutes, stirring, until it reads 165F. If it is the ground chicken, brown it in a hot skillet with a little oil over medium-high, 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up, until no pink remains and it reads 165F. If it is the leg quarters, roast them at 425F for 35 to 45 minutes, until 165F near the bone, then pull the meat off the bone, leave the skin behind and chop it.\n4. Toss the chicken with the salsa so it turns saucy.\n5. Slice your vegetables and cook the slices in the same pan 3 to 4 minutes, until soft and lightly charred.\n6. Build the bowl with your carb on the bottom, the saucy chicken and vegetables on top, then shower it with shredded cheddar and let it melt from the heat.",
  "oil": "Cheddar is the fat in this dish, melted over the top for that enchilada richness. For cooking, sear the chicken in just a spray or teaspoon of avocado oil (about 520F smoke point) so it browns at high heat without smoking, the cheese does the flavor work, so the cooking oil stays neutral and minimal.",
