 "method": "1. Cook the barley: rinse it, then simmer it in 3 cups of water per cup, 25 to 30 minutes, until tender but still chewy, and drain it. Weigh it cooked.\n2. Drain and rinse your protein (white beans, navy beans or chickpeas), which washes off the canning salt.\n3. Heat a little oil in a wide pan over medium heat and soften a little diced onion and 1 minced garlic clove 2 to 3 minutes.\n4. Stir your protein and the barley into the pan, then add warm broth one ladle at a time, stirring and letting each addition soak in before the next, 6 to 8 minutes, until creamy and loose, as in a risotto.\n5. If your vegetables include the spinach, stir it in for the last 1 to 2 minutes, until wilted. If it is the kale, chop it and stir it in for the last 4 to 5 minutes, until tender.\n6. Take the pan off the heat. Beat in the parmesan so the risotto turns glossy and rich. If your fat is the olive oil, finish with a drizzle of your fat. Serve loose, not stiff.",
 "oil": "The parmesan beaten in at the end (if you eat dairy) is the second fat and gives that creamy, cheesy risotto finish without any cream.",
