  "method": "1. Make the slaw: thinly slice, shred or dice your vegetables, toss them with the juice of 1/2 lime and a pinch of salt, and let them sit while you cook, so they soften a little.\n2. Mix the rub: 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp chili powder, 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp oregano, 1/4 tsp salt, 1/4 tsp pepper and a pinch of cayenne.\n3. Heat a heavy skillet with a little oil over high heat 2 to 3 minutes, until very hot, because the crust needs a hot pan.\n4. If your protein is the canned mackerel, drain it and break it into big chunks. Pat your protein dry so the rub sticks, press the rub on all sides and sear it 2 to 3 minutes a side without moving it, until the crust is dark and it flakes and reads 145F. Break it into big chunks.\n5. Warm your carb in a dry pan 20 to 30 seconds a side, until soft and lightly charred, so it folds without cracking.\n6. Fill each taco with slaw and chunks of your protein, then top with the salsa and the cheddar. If your fat is the avocado, slice it on top. Finish with a squeeze of lime.",
  "oil": "Cook in avocado oil (smoke point ~520F). Blackening needs a screaming-hot pan, and avocado oil takes that heat without smoking or turning the spices bitter. Skip olive oil or butter here, they would scorch. If your plan lists avocado (not the oil) as the fat, slice it on at the end as a cool, creamy finish instead.",
  "season": "Blackening rub (optional but classic): smoked paprika, cumin, garlic powder, onion powder, dried oregano, salt, black pepper, and a little cayenne for heat. A big squeeze of fresh lime over the finished tacos ties it all together. Fresh cilantro on top if you have it.",
