  "method": "1. Start your grain first. Weigh it cooked. If your grain is the wild rice, simmer it covered in 3 cups water per cup of rice 45 to 55 minutes, until the grains split open. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups water per cup of rice 40 to 45 minutes. If it is the quinoa, rinse it and simmer it covered in 2 cups water per cup of quinoa 15 minutes. If it is the riced cauliflower, cook it covered in a nonstick pan over medium heat 4 to 5 minutes, until tender.\n2. Dice your vegetables small, melt your fat in a pot over medium heat and sweat them 7 to 8 minutes, until soft.\n3. Stir in 3 cloves minced garlic and 1 tsp thyme for 30 seconds, then pour in 5 cups of chicken broth and bring it to a gentle simmer, because a hard boil toughens the chicken.\n4. Add your protein whole, cover and simmer, 15 to 25 minutes for boneless pieces or 35 to 40 minutes for bone-in ones, until no longer pink and 165F in the thickest part. Lift it out, shred it with two forks, discard any bones and skin, and return it to the pot.\n5. Stir in your grain and warm it 3 to 4 minutes, then add a splash of milk, a squeeze of lemon and a pinch of salt and pepper.\n6. Ladle the soup into bowls and top with the parmesan.",
  "oil": "A small pat of salted butter over medium heat gives the soup its cozy, rich backbone. Butter's milk solids brown past ~350F, but this is a low-and-slow sweat, not a sear, so it never gets near that point. Olive oil works if you want to skip the dairy.",
