  "method": "1. Start your grain first. Weigh it cooked. If your grain is the white rice, simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups water per cup of rice 18 minutes and rest it 5 minutes. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups water per cup of rice 40 to 45 minutes. If it is the quinoa, rinse it and simmer it covered in 2 cups water per cup of quinoa 15 minutes. If it is the riced cauliflower, cook it covered in a nonstick pan over medium heat 4 to 5 minutes, until tender.\n2. If your protein is the tofu, press it 10 minutes between paper towels under something heavy so it crisps, cube it and sear it in a little oil over medium-high heat 8 to 10 minutes, turning, until golden on all sides. If it is the TVP, soak it in hot water 10 minutes, squeeze it dry and brown it in a little oil 5 to 6 minutes, until crisp at the edges.\n3. Set your protein aside, then stir-fry your vegetables in the same hot pan 3 to 4 minutes, until crisp tender.\n4. Whisk the peanut sauce with 1 tbsp tamari, 1 tsp sriracha, a squeeze of lime and a splash of water until pourable. If your fat is the peanut butter, whisk it in too.\n5. Return your protein to the pan, pour in the sauce and toss 1 minute, until coated.\n6. Spoon it over your grain and finish with 1 tbsp chopped cilantro.",
  "oil": "Sear the tofu in avocado oil (smoke point ~520F) so it crisps hard at high heat without smoking; canola (~450F) works too. The peanut butter is the real flavor fat here, whisked raw into the sauce off the heat, so keep the pan fat to a light coat. Don't sear in olive oil (~375F), it would scorch before the tofu browns.",
