  "method": "1. Rinse the barley and simmer it covered in 3 cups of water per cup of barley, 25 to 30 minutes, until chewy and tender, then drain it. Weigh it cooked.\n2. Heat a little of the olive oil in a wide pan over medium heat. If it is the onion, dice it and cook it 4 to 5 minutes, until soft. If it is the carrots, dice them small and cook them 5 to 6 minutes, until tender. Add 3 minced garlic cloves and 1/2 tsp rosemary and cook 1 minute, until fragrant, so the garlic does not scorch.\n3. Drain and rinse your beans and add them to the pan with a splash of water. If it is the tomato, dice it and add it too. Simmer 6 to 8 minutes, smashing a few beans against the pan, so the broth turns creamy.\n4. If it is the kale, chop it and stir it in for the last 3 to 4 minutes, until it wilts and turns bright.\n5. Spoon the beans over the barley, top with the feta and olives, and finish with the rest of the olive oil, a squeeze of lemon and a pinch of chili flakes.",
  "oil": "Extra-virgin olive oil (smoke point ~375F) is the heart of Tuscan cooking, use it for the medium-heat soffritto and again raw as a finishing drizzle. Both jobs sit comfortably under its smoke point. Keep the pan at medium and never push it to a hard sear, or the oil turns bitter.",
