  "method": "1. Heat the oven to 400F. If it is the falafel, bake it on a tray 10 to 12 minutes, turning once, until crisp and hot through. If it is the chickpeas, drain and rinse them, pat them dry, toss them with 1 tsp cumin and a pinch of salt, and roast them 15 to 20 minutes, until firm and golden.\n2. While your protein bakes, cook your grain. If it is the bulgur, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of bulgur, 12 to 15 minutes, until tender. If it is the couscous, pour over an equal amount of boiling water, cover it and leave it 5 to 7 minutes, until fluffy. Weigh it cooked, then toss it with 2 tbsp chopped parsley, 1 tbsp chopped mint, a squeeze of lemon and a pinch of salt while it is still warm, so it soaks up the flavor.\n3. Dice your vegetables small and toss them with a squeeze of lemon and a pinch of salt.\n4. Make the sauce. If your fat is the tahini, thin it with lemon juice and a splash of water, until pourable. If it is the hummus, loosen it with a splash of water. If it is the olive oil, whisk it with lemon juice and a pinch of salt.\n5. Spoon the herbed grain into a bowl and add your protein. Pile your vegetables on one side and finish with your fat.",
  "oil": "Tahini (and the scoop of hummus) is the raw finishing fat here, thinned with lemon and water into a sauce, no heat needed. If you pan-crisp the falafel instead of baking, use a little extra-virgin olive oil at medium heat (smoke point ~375F); baking or roasting at 400F needs no extra oil.",
