  "method": "1. Prick the potato all over and microwave it 5 to 7 minutes, turning once, until a knife slides in easily. Weigh it cooked, then dice it small.\n2. Heat the broiler to high, so the top of the frittata sets without flipping it. Heat the olive oil in an oven-safe skillet over medium heat and crisp the potato 6 to 8 minutes, stirring now and then, until golden.\n3. Add the spinach and stir 1 to 2 minutes, until it wilts.\n4. If it is the feta, crumble it over the potato and spinach.\n5. If your protein is eggs or egg whites, beat them with a pinch of salt and pepper, pour them evenly over the potato and spinach, cook over medium-low heat 3 to 4 minutes, until the edges set, then broil 4 to 5 minutes, until the center is just set (160F).\n6. Slice the frittata into wedges and serve with a drizzle of the hot sauce and a little dill.",
  "oil": "Olive oil (smoke point ~375F) handles the medium-heat potato crisp and the gentle egg set without smoking; keep it at medium so the eggs stay custardy. If you want a harder potato crisp first, start in avocado oil (smoke point ~520F) over medium-high heat, then drop to gentle heat for the eggs. Avoid a hot butter sear here, its milk solids would brown before the eggs set.",
