  "method": "1. Cook your protein. If it is the yellowfin tuna, season it with salt and pepper and sear it in a little oil over medium-high heat 2 to 3 minutes a side, until opaque and 145F in the center, then flake it. If it is the light tuna, drain it very well and flake it. If it is the canned mackerel, drain it very well and flake it.\n2. Let your protein cool a few minutes in a bowl, so the mayonnaise stays creamy.\n3. Fold in the mayonnaise a spoonful at a time, until just creamy.\n4. Finely dice the pickles and your vegetables and stir them in, with 1 tsp mustard and a squeeze of lemon.\n5. Toast your carb 2 to 3 minutes, until golden, so it does not go soggy.\n6. Mound the salad on one slice, close it with the second and slice it in half.",
