  "note": "Dak galbi is a Korean stir-fry of gluten-free gochujang-marinated chicken and cabbage. Lean chicken keeps protein high while the cabbage and onion bulk the bowl for very few calories.",
  "method": "1. Start your grain. If it is the white rice, rinse it, simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice for about 18 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat, then weigh it cooked. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice for about 40 minutes, rest it 10 minutes off the heat, then weigh it cooked. If it is the quinoa, rinse it, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa for about 15 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat, then weigh it cooked. If it is the riced cauliflower, cook it in a hot skillet for 3 to 5 minutes, stirring, until tender, then weigh it cooked.\n2. Stir the gochujang, soy sauce, honey and grated garlic into a thick red marinade.\n3. Cut your protein into bite-size chunks, off the bone if it has one, then toss it in the marinade and leave it 10 minutes, so the flavor soaks in.\n4. Slice your vegetables thin, so they cook in the same few minutes as your protein. If it is the cabbage, shred it fine.\n5. Heat a little oil in a wide pan over medium-high, add your protein with its marinade and stir-fry 5 to 6 minutes, until the edges char and it is cooked through (165F).\n6. Add your vegetables and stir-fry 3 to 4 minutes more, until they wilt but keep some bite.\n7. Spoon your grain into a bowl, pile your protein and vegetables on top and scrape the pan sauce over it. Finish with black pepper and a little sriracha if you want more heat.",
