 "season": "Optional: a generous pile of fresh ginger and scallion (the whole dish), garlic, tamari, and a spoon of hot oil poured over at the end. A few drops of toasted sesame oil to finish. A splash of rice vinegar or a squeeze of lime at the table to lift the soy.",
 "note": "Cantonese steamed fish with a hot-oil-over-scallions finish, one of the leanest restaurant dishes there is. Mild white fish makes it nearly pure protein over rice and greens.",
 "method": "1. Start your grain. If it is the white rice, rinse it, simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice for about 18 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat, then weigh it cooked. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice for about 40 minutes, rest it 10 minutes off the heat, then weigh it cooked. If it is the quinoa, rinse it, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa for about 15 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat, then weigh it cooked. If it is the riced cauliflower, cook it in a hot skillet for 3 to 5 minutes, stirring, until tender, then weigh it cooked.\n2. Cut 3 scallions into long thin shreds and 1 inch of ginger into fine matchsticks.\n3. If your protein is the canned mackerel, drain and rinse it. Set your protein on a heatproof plate. If it is the cod, set the plate in a steamer over simmering water, cover and steam 8 to 10 minutes, until it flakes (145F). If it is the haddock, set the plate in a steamer over simmering water, cover and steam 8 to 10 minutes, until it flakes (145F). If it is the tilapia, set the plate in a steamer over simmering water, cover and steam 6 to 8 minutes, until it flakes (145F).\n4. Meanwhile, cut your vegetables into thin pieces and simmer them in a pot of water 2 to 4 minutes, until tender, then drain them.\n5. Stir the soy sauce, coconut aminos and grated garlic together.\n6. Pile the scallion and ginger on your protein. Heat a little oil in a small pan until it just shimmers, then pour it over them, so they sizzle and release their aroma. Spoon the sauce around your protein.\n7. Spoon your grain into a bowl, add your vegetables and lay your protein on top with all the sauce.",
