  "produce": "Tomato raw|Bell pepper red raw",
  "season": "Optional: onion, Turkish pepper paste (biber salcasi) or a pinch of Aleppo pepper, paprika, dried oregano, salt, and black pepper. Finish with fresh parsley; go easy on salt with the feta.",
  "note": "Classic Turkish breakfast. Keep the yolks runny so they mix into the tomato and pepper base. Eat it family-style straight from the pan.",
  "method": "1. Finely chop 1 small onion and dice your vegetables small, so they melt into a sauce.\n2. Heat the olive oil in a nonstick pan over medium, add the onion and cook 4 to 5 minutes, stirring, until soft.\n3. Add 1 tsp paprika, a pinch of salt, a pinch of pepper and your vegetables, then simmer gently 8 to 10 minutes, until they break down into a thick sauce, because a watery base turns the eggs soggy.\n4. Crumble the feta over the sauce and let it warm 1 minute.\n5. Crack the eggs into the pan and nudge them gently with a spoon, so the whites mix into the sauce. Cook 3 to 4 minutes, until set with no runny parts (160F).\n6. Warm your carb in a dry pan or toaster, about 30 seconds a side, until hot and soft.\n7. Sprinkle the eggs with dried oregano and a little more pepper, then tear your carb into pieces and scoop up the eggs and sauce straight from the pan.",
