  "season": "garlic, smoked paprika, red pepper flakes, salt, black pepper, dried parsley, lemon juice if you have it",
  "note": "A tapas-bar classic turned into a full plate. The shrimp and white beans both bring protein, and the smoked paprika garlic oil carries the flavor, so measure the oil.",
  "method": "1. Pat the shrimp very dry, then season with salt, pepper and 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, so they sear instead of steaming.\n2. Drain and rinse the white beans. Mince 3 to 4 cloves of garlic.\n3. Heat the olive oil in a wide skillet over medium. Add the garlic and a pinch of chili flakes and cook about 45 seconds, until pale gold and fragrant, because browned garlic turns bitter.\n4. Turn the heat to medium-high, add the shrimp in one flat layer and cook 1 1/2 to 2 minutes a side, until pink, curled and opaque (145F). Scoop them onto a plate.\n5. Prep and cook your vegetables in the same pan. If it is the red bell pepper, slice it thin and cook it 4 minutes, until soft. If it is the spinach, wash it and cook it 2 minutes, until wilted.\n6. Stir in the white beans and cook 2 to 3 minutes, until hot.\n7. Return the shrimp and toss 30 seconds, so the garlic oil coats everything, then add a squeeze of lemon and a sprinkle of parsley.\n8. Warm the pita in a dry pan, 20 seconds a side. Spoon the shrimp and beans into a bowl and serve with the pita for scooping up the garlic oil.",
