  "prefProduce": "Bell pepper red raw",
  "cuisine": "Spanish/tapas",
  "season": "Optional: smoked paprika (pimenton, the chorizo backbone), garlic, ground cumin, dried oregano, a pinch of cayenne, salt, and black pepper, with a splash of sherry or red wine vinegar to finish.",
  "note": "This hits the smoky, garlicky chorizo-and-patatas flavor of a Spanish tapas plate using lean pork and a spice rub instead of fatty sausage, so the protein stays high and the fat stays controlled.",
  "method": "1. Cut the potato into small half-inch cubes, so they cook through fast.\n2. Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high. Add the potato cubes with a pinch of salt and cook 12 to 15 minutes, stirring now and then, until golden and a fork slides in easily. Push them to one side.\n3. While the potatoes cook, stir 1 tbsp smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp cumin, 1 tsp oregano, 2 cloves minced garlic, 1/2 tsp salt, 1/2 tsp pepper and a pinch of cayenne into a rub. Cut your protein into bite-size pieces, off the bone if it has one, and toss it with half of the rub.\n4. Slice your vegetables thin, add them to the open side of the pan and cook 4 to 5 minutes, until they soften and pick up some color. Stir in the rest of the rub.\n5. Add your protein and cook 4 to 5 minutes, stirring, until browned at the edges and cooked through (145F).\n6. Splash in a little red wine vinegar and scrape up the brown bits from the pan, so they melt into the sauce.\n7. Pile it all on a plate and serve hot.",
