  "season": "garlic, dried oregano, salt, black pepper, lemon juice, red wine vinegar if you have it",
  "note": "A taverna plate. The lemon-oregano potatoes and chunky feta salad do the heavy flavor lifting, so the lean lamb chop can stay a sensible portion while the meal still tastes rich.",
  "method": "1. Heat the oven to 425F. Cut the potato into wedges and toss with a little of the olive oil, 1 tsp dried oregano, 1 minced garlic clove, the juice of 1/2 lemon and a pinch of salt and pepper.\n2. Spread the potato wedges in one layer and roast 30 to 35 minutes, turning once, until golden at the edges and a fork slides in easily.\n3. While they roast, chop your vegetables into chunks for the village salad and add a few slices of onion and the olives. Dress with a little of the olive oil, 1 tsp red wine vinegar, 1/2 tsp dried oregano and a pinch of salt.\n4. Crumble the feta over the salad and fold once, so the feta stays in chunks.\n5. Season your protein on both sides with 1/2 tsp dried oregano, 1/2 tsp minced garlic and a pinch of salt and pepper.\n6. Heat a thin film of the olive oil in a skillet over medium-high until it shimmers, then sear your protein 3 to 5 minutes a side, until the center reads 145F.\n7. Rest it on a plate for 5 minutes, so the juices stay in the meat instead of running out.\n8. Plate your protein next to the potatoes, pile the village salad beside it and finish with a squeeze of lemon over the whole plate.",
