  "season": "Optional: smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, chili powder, a pinch of brown sugar, salt, and black pepper as a rub, then glaze with BBQ sauce in the last few minutes. Cayenne for heat.",
  "note": "A steakhouse-style loaded baked potato made the lean way. The Greek yogurt stands in for sour cream and the reduced-fat cheddar keeps the gooey factor, so it eats like a treat while the protein stays high.",
  "method": "1. Heat the oven to 425F. Prick the potato all over with a fork and bake it 45 to 55 minutes, until a fork slides in with no resistance.\n2. Mix the rub: 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp onion powder, 1/2 tsp chili powder, a pinch of cayenne, 1/2 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp black pepper. Rub it over your protein with a little oil, so the spices stick and the outside browns.\n3. Roast your protein on a tray beside the potato until the thickest part reads 165F. If it is the chicken breast, it needs 20 to 25 minutes, so add it when the potato has 25 minutes left. If it is the chicken thigh, it needs 25 to 30 minutes, so add it when the potato has 30 minutes left. If it is the chicken leg quarter, it needs 40 to 45 minutes, so add it when the potato has 45 minutes left.\n4. Brush the BBQ sauce over the chicken for the last 3 minutes, so it turns sticky without burning.\n5. While it roasts, steam your vegetables in a covered pan with a splash of water, 4 to 5 minutes, until bright and just tender, then season with a pinch of salt and pepper.\n6. Rest the chicken 5 minutes, then chop or slice it, so the juices stay in.\n7. Split the potato and fluff the inside with a fork. Pile the chicken on top, add a spoon of the Greek yogurt and scatter the cheddar over the hot chicken so it melts.\n8. Serve with the vegetables on the side.",
