  "method": "1. In a jar or bowl, stir together the oats, the pea and rice protein powder and your nut butter.\n2. Add 3/4 cup of unsweetened almond milk a splash at a time, stirring well so the powder mixes in without clumping. It should look like a loose pudding, so add a little more milk if it is stiff, because the oats keep soaking up liquid overnight.\n3. Slice the banana on top.\n4. Cover and chill it in the fridge overnight, or at least 4 hours, so the oats soften and the mix turns thick and creamy. In a hurry, leave it on the counter 30 minutes instead, and expect it to be chewier.\n5. In the morning, give it a stir, add a pinch of cinnamon and eat it cold."
