  "oil": "Heat a teaspoon of olive oil in a nonstick pan over medium heat to keep the tofu from sticking and to crisp the edges.",
  "season": "Optional: turmeric plus a pinch of black salt (kala namak) makes it taste eggy, with garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, salt, and pepper. Nutritional yeast adds a savory, cheesy note.",
  "note": "A savory vegan breakfast that actually hits protein: crumbled tofu plus black beans plus a potato base. The turmeric and black salt give it a real scrambled-egg flavor.",
  "method": "1. Start your carb first, since it takes the longest. If your carb is the potato, prick it all over and microwave it on high 6 to 8 minutes, turning once, until a fork slides in easily. If it is the sweet potato, prick it all over and microwave it on high 6 to 8 minutes, turning once, until a fork slides in easily. If it is the oats, measure them dry, then simmer them in 2 cups of water per cup of oats, 5 to 7 minutes, until thick and creamy.\n2. While your carb cooks, prep your protein. If it is the tofu, press it 10 minutes between paper towels with a weight on top, so it does not steam the scramble, then crumble it into small pieces. If it is the tempeh, crumble it into small pieces.\n3. Heat a little oil in a nonstick pan over medium. Add your protein and cook 6 to 8 minutes, stirring now and then, until golden at the edges and the water has cooked off.\n4. Stir in 1/2 tsp turmeric, 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp cumin and a pinch of salt, so the scramble turns yellow and savory.\n5. Chop your vegetables and add them with the black beans, drained and rinsed. Cook 2 to 3 minutes, until the vegetables soften or wilt and the beans are hot.\n6. Spoon the scramble over your carb and top with the salsa verde, the hot sauce and your fat."
