  "note": "A lighter take on Japanese soba. Buckwheat groats stand in for soba noodles, tossed with lean chicken and crisp veg in a sugar-free gluten-free teriyaki glaze.",
  "method": "1. Start your carb first. If your carb is the buckwheat groats, rinse them and simmer covered in 2 cups of water per cup of groats, 12 to 15 minutes, until tender and the water is absorbed, then weigh them cooked. If it is the whole wheat pasta, boil it in plenty of salted water 8 to 10 minutes, until al dente, then drain it and weigh it cooked. If it is the chickpea pasta, boil it in plenty of salted water 6 to 8 minutes, until al dente, then drain it and weigh it cooked.\n2. Slice your protein into thin strips, so it cooks fast and evenly, and season with a pinch of salt and pepper.\n3. Heat the avocado oil in a large pan over medium-high. Add your protein and cook 5 to 7 minutes, stirring now and then, until golden, no longer pink and 165F in the thickest piece.\n4. Add your vegetables, cut into bite-size pieces, with 1 tsp grated ginger and 1 minced garlic clove. Stir-fry 3 to 4 minutes, until bright and just tender.\n5. Pour in the teriyaki sauce and the soy sauce and toss 1 minute, until everything is glossy.\n6. Add your carb and toss 1 more minute to warm it through.\n7. Serve warm, topped with sliced scallion and a sprinkle of sesame seeds.",
