  "method": "1. Rinse the quinoa, then simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, 15 minutes, until the water is absorbed. Rest it 5 minutes off the heat, fluff it and let it cool. Weigh it cooked.\n2. Slice the turkey breast into thin cutlets, pat them dry and sear them in a little oil in a skillet over medium-high heat 4 to 5 minutes a side, until no longer pink inside (165F).\n3. Rest the turkey 5 minutes, then dice it.\n4. Boil the green peas in a small pot 2 to 3 minutes, until bright green and tender, then drain them and rinse them under cold water, so they stay firm.\n5. Drain and rinse the kidney beans and chickpeas, then pat them dry, so the dressing clings.\n6. In a big bowl, whisk the olive oil, 2 tsp cider vinegar, the honey, salt and pepper.\n7. Add the beans, peas, diced celery, diced onion and turkey and toss until coated, then fold in the quinoa.\n8. Cover and chill it in the fridge overnight, or at least 4 hours, so the beans drink up the dressing. In a hurry, let it sit on the counter 30 minutes.\n9. Stir again, scatter chopped parsley over the top and serve cold.",
