 "method": "1. Warm the olive oil in a wide pan over medium heat, add the finely chopped onion, carrot and celery and cook 7 minutes, until soft.\n2. Stir in the minced garlic and the zucchini and cook 4 minutes, until the zucchini gives up its liquid and it cooks off.\n3. Stir in 1 tbsp tomato paste and 1 tsp oregano and cook 2 minutes, because toasting the paste deepens the flavor.\n4. Drain and rinse the lentils, then add them with the marinara and a splash of water and simmer 12 minutes over medium-low heat, until thick.\n5. While the sauce simmers, cook your carb. If your carb is the whole wheat pasta, boil it in salted water 9 to 11 minutes, until al dente, then drain it and weigh it cooked. If it is the chickpea pasta, boil it 7 to 9 minutes, until al dente, then drain it and weigh it cooked.\n6. Stir 1 tsp red wine vinegar into the sauce, toss it with your carb and serve.",
 "oil": "Olive oil"
