  "method": "1. If it is the potato, heat the oven to 425F, cut it into 1-inch cubes, toss with a little oil and salt, and roast on a sheet pan 25 to 30 minutes, until golden and a fork slides in.\n2. If it is the sweet potato, heat the oven to 425F, cut it into 1-inch cubes, toss with a little oil and salt, and roast on a sheet pan 20 to 25 minutes, until the edges caramelize and a fork slides in.\n3. If it is the quinoa, rinse it and simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, 12 to 15 minutes, until the water is gone, then rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked.\n4. If it is the chicken breast, slice it in half through the middle into two thin cutlets, so it cooks through evenly without drying out.\n5. Season your protein all over with salt, pepper, 1/2 tsp garlic powder and 1/2 tsp paprika.\n6. Heat a grill pan or skillet over medium-high with a little oil and cook your protein 5 to 7 minutes per side, until browned and 165F in the thickest part, then rest it 5 minutes.\n7. While it rests, cut your vegetables into bite-size pieces and steam them 4 to 5 minutes, until bright and just tender.\n8. Simmer the edamame in a small pot of water 3 to 5 minutes, until bright green and tender, then drain it.\n9. Plate your protein with the edamame, your carb and your vegetables, and finish with a squeeze of lemon.",
  "season": "Garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, salt, and pepper on the chicken. A squeeze of lemon at the end.",
  "note": "Chicken, a simple grain or potato, a green vegetable, and edamame on the side. Easy to batch-cook.",
