  "method": "1. If it is the turkey breast, season it with salt, pepper, 1/2 tsp garlic powder and 1/2 tsp sage, roast it ahead (375F, 25 to 35 minutes for a thick cutlet, until 165F in the thickest part) or use leftover, then slice it and warm the slices in a pan with a splash of broth for 2 minutes so they stay moist.\n2. If it is the chicken breast, slice it in half through the middle into two cutlets, season with salt, pepper, 1/2 tsp garlic powder and 1/2 tsp sage, then cook in a hot oiled pan over medium heat 5 to 6 minutes per side, until browned and 165F in the thickest part.\n3. If it is the sweet potato, prick it and cook it in the microwave 5 to 7 minutes, turning once, until a fork slides in easily.\n4. If it is the potato, prick it and cook it in the microwave 6 to 8 minutes, turning once, until a fork slides in easily.\n5. If it is the quinoa, rinse it and simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, 12 to 15 minutes, until the water is gone, then rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked.\n6. If it is the broccoli, cut it into small florets and steam it 4 to 5 minutes, until bright green and just tender. If it is the green beans, snap off the stem ends and steam them 4 to 5 minutes, until just tender. If it is the asparagus, snap off the woody ends and steam it 3 to 4 minutes, until tender-crisp.\n7. Serve your protein with your carb and your vegetables, with a squeeze of lemon over the vegetables.",
  "season": "Garlic powder, poultry seasoning or sage, salt, and pepper.",
