  "method": "1. Cook the quinoa: rinse it, then simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa, 12 to 15 minutes, until the water is gone, and rest it 5 minutes off the heat. Weigh it cooked.\n2. Whisk 1 tbsp honey, 1 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tsp minced garlic and 1 tsp rice vinegar in a small bowl, because the vinegar balances the honey.\n3. Cut the chicken breast into 1-inch pieces and season with salt and pepper, so the pieces cook evenly.\n4. Heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium-high and cook the chicken 5 to 6 minutes, turning now and then, until browned and 165F in the center.\n5. Pour in the sauce and let it bubble 1 to 2 minutes, until it coats the chicken, then take the pan off the heat, because honey scorches fast.\n6. Cut the broccoli into small florets and steam it 4 to 5 minutes, until bright green and just tender.\n7. Simmer the edamame in a small pot of water 3 to 5 minutes, until bright green and tender, then drain it.\n8. Serve the chicken and broccoli over the quinoa, with the edamame on the side.",
