 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large deep skillet, a small dry pan, a sheet pan or a pot for your carb, a knife, a wooden spoon, a meat thermometer and 5 containers.\n2. Cook your carb first: if it is the sweet potato, peel it, cut it into 1/2-inch cubes, mist them with cooking spray, salt them, and roast at 400F 25 to 30 minutes, until soft; if it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup, 40 to 45 minutes, until the water is absorbed. Weigh it cooked.\n3. Toast 2 tsp chili powder, 2 tsp ground cumin, 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1 tsp dried oregano and 1/2 tsp ground coriander in the dry pan over medium 1 minute, until fragrant, then tip them into a bowl.\n4. If it is the bell pepper, dice it into 1/2-inch pieces. If it is the onion, dice it into 1/2-inch pieces. If it is the black beans, drain and rinse them, because canned beans come cooked.\n5. Heat the olive oil in the skillet over medium-high. If it is the bell pepper, cook it 5 minutes, until soft. If it is the onion, cook it 5 minutes, until the edges turn translucent.\n6. Push the vegetables aside and add the ground beef to the bare metal. Leave it 2 minutes so it browns, because that crust is the flavor, then break it up, salt it with 1 tsp salt, and cook 6 to 8 minutes more, until no pink remains and it reads 160F.\n7. Stir in the toasted spices and 1/2 cup of water and simmer 3 to 4 minutes, until the beef is glossy. If it is the black beans, stir them in now and heat them 2 minutes.\n8. Off the heat, stir in the juice of 1 lime and a handful of chopped cilantro.\n9. Divide your carb between the 5 containers and spoon the beef over it. If your fat is the cheddar, scatter it over each now so it melts into the beef when warmed.\n10. Keep the avocado and the salsa separate, because cut avocado browns.\n11. Cool with the lids off until the steam stops, about 20 minutes, then seal, date, and refrigerate within 1 hour, because cooked starches spoil fast.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months; freeze on the cook day any container not eaten by day 4.\n13. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes with a splash of water, stirring halfway, or 4 to 5 minutes from frozen, then add the avocado and salsa.",
