 "method": "Microwave one container 2 minutes with a splash of water, stir, then add fresh avocado and a spoon of pico after heating.",
 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large pot with a lid or a slow cooker, a small pot with a lid, two forks, a knife, a fine strainer, a meat thermometer and 5 containers.\n2. Rub the chicken breasts all over with 1 tsp salt and let them sit 10 minutes while you set up, so the salt reaches the middle and the meat holds its juices.\n3. Put the chicken in the pot with the salsa verde, 1 cup of broth, 1 tsp ground cumin, 1 tsp garlic powder and 1/2 tsp dried oregano.\n4. Bring it to a gentle simmer, cover, and cook on low 22 to 28 minutes, flipping once, until the thickest piece reads 165F and pulls apart easily (slow cooker: 4 hours on low).\n5. Lift the chicken onto the board, rest it 5 minutes so the juices settle, then shred it with the forks and stir it back into the pot juices so it soaks them up.\n6. Cook the quinoa while the chicken simmers: rinse it until the water runs clear, because its coating tastes bitter, then simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup, 15 minutes, until the water is absorbed. Rest it 5 minutes and fluff it. Weigh it cooked.\n7. Cook the sweet corn from frozen, 3 to 4 minutes in boiling water, and drain it.\n8. If it is the bell pepper, dice it small and keep it raw for crunch. If it is the black beans, drain and rinse them; canned beans come cooked.\n9. Divide the quinoa between the 5 containers, then the chicken with its sauce, the corn and your produce. If your fat is the cheddar, scatter it over each now, because it melts in when you warm it up.\n10. Keep the avocado separate, because cut avocado browns; it goes on after reheating.\n11. Cool with the lids off until the steam stops, about 20 to 30 minutes, then seal, date each one, and refrigerate within 1 hour, because cooked grains spoil fast.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months. Freeze on the cook day any container not eaten by day 4, and thaw it in the fridge overnight.\n13. Reheat: microwave 2 minutes with a splash of water, stirring halfway, or 4 to 5 minutes from frozen. Add the avocado, a squeeze of lime and chopped cilantro after heating.",
