 "method": "Microwave one container 2 to 3 minutes, stir, then top with avocado and a little shredded cheddar after heating.",
 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large pot, a small pot, a knife, a wooden spoon, a can opener, a meat thermometer and 5 containers.\n2. Cook the lentils if they are on your list: simmer them in 3 cups of water per cup, 18 to 25 minutes, until tender, then drain them. Weigh them cooked.\n3. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup, 40 to 45 minutes, until the water is absorbed; weigh it cooked.\n4. Prepare your produce: if it is the onion, dice it; if it is the bell pepper, dice it; if it is the kidney beans, drain and rinse them.\n5. Toast 2 tsp chili powder, 2 tsp ground cumin, 1 tsp smoked paprika and 1 tsp dried oregano in the dry pot over medium 1 minute, until fragrant, then tip them into a bowl.\n6. Add a little oil to the pot over medium-high. If it is the onion, cook it 5 minutes, until soft. If it is the bell pepper, cook it 5 minutes, until soft. Add 3 minced garlic cloves for 30 seconds.\n7. Cook your protein: if it is the ground turkey, brown it in the hot pot 2 minutes before breaking it up, then salt it and cook 6 to 8 minutes more, until no pink remains and it reads 165F; if it is the lentils, stir the cooked lentils in with 1 tsp salt.\n8. Stir in the toasted spices, 3 cups of broth, 1 tsp minced chipotle in adobo, 1 tbsp vinegar and 1 tbsp hot sauce. If it is the kidney beans, stir them in. If it is the canned pumpkin, stir it in; it gives the chili its body.\n9. Simmer uncovered 20 to 25 minutes, stirring now and then, until a spoon dragged across the bottom leaves a trail.\n10. Off the heat, stir in the juice of 1 lime and 1 tbsp maple to round out the heat, then taste for salt.\n11. Divide the chili between the 5 containers. If it is the brown rice, put it in each container first. Keep the avocado and the cheddar separate for after reheating.\n12. Cool with the lids off until the steam stops, about 20 minutes, then seal, date, and refrigerate within 1 hour, because cooked grains and lentils spoil fast.\n13. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months; chili freezes well.\n14. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes, stirring once, or 5 to 6 minutes from frozen, until steaming hot, then add the avocado and the cheddar.",
