 "method": "Reheat in an air fryer or 400F oven 6 to 8 minutes to re-crisp, or microwave 2 minutes if you do not mind it soft. Crumble feta on after heating.",
 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: two large rimmed sheet pans, parchment, a cutting board, a knife, a large bowl, paper towels, a meat thermometer and 4 containers. Heat the oven to 425F, because high heat caramelizes the sweet potato and crisps the edges.\n2. Peel the sweet potatoes and cut them into 3/4-inch cubes, so they roast through in the same time as the chicken.\n3. Prepare your produce: if it is the bell pepper, cut it into 1-inch chunks; if it is the onion, cut it into 1-inch wedges; if it is the chickpeas, drain and rinse them and pat them very dry with paper towels, because dry chickpeas crisp and wet ones steam.\n4. Toss the sweet potato and your produce in the bowl with half the olive oil, 1 tbsp harissa paste, 1 tsp ground cumin, 1/2 tsp ground coriander and 1/2 tsp salt, and spread them across both lined pans in a single layer with space between pieces, because crowded food steams instead of roasting.\n5. Pat the chicken thighs dry on both sides, because a dry surface browns, then rub them with 1 more tbsp harissa, the rest of the olive oil, 1/2 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, and nestle them among the vegetables.\n6. Roast 25 to 30 minutes, until the sweet potato is fork-tender, the edges are deep golden, and a thermometer in the thickest chicken thigh reads 165F.\n7. Rest the chicken 5 minutes on the pan so the juices settle back into the meat, then squeeze the juice of 1 lemon over everything and scatter chopped parsley or mint.\n8. Divide the chicken and the vegetables between the 4 containers. Keep the feta separate in a small tub per serving, because it goes grainy when it is heated.\n9. Cool the containers with the lids off until they stop steaming, about 20 to 30 minutes, then seal them, write the date on each, and refrigerate within 2 hours of cooking.\n10. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months, though the chickpeas and the potato soften after freezing, so eat the fridge portions first.\n11. Reheat: air fryer or 400F oven 6 to 8 minutes to crisp the edges back up, or microwave 2 minutes if you do not mind it soft. Crumble the feta over the top after heating.",
