 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large sheet pan, parchment, a steamer basket, a small pot with a lid, a fine strainer, a small bowl, a whisk, a knife and 4 containers. Heat the oven to 425F.\n2. Steam the tempeh whole over simmering water 8 to 10 minutes, then pat it dry and cut it into 1/2-inch cubes; steaming takes away its bitter edge so it soaks up the glaze.\n3. Cook the quinoa: rinse it until the water runs clear, because its coating tastes bitter, then simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup, 15 minutes, until the water is absorbed. Fluff it and spread it on a tray to cool. Weigh it cooked.\n4. Make the glaze: whisk 2 tbsp gochujang, 2 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tbsp maple syrup, 1 tbsp rice vinegar, 1 tsp grated ginger and 1 minced garlic clove. If your fat is the sesame oil, whisk 1 tbsp of it in too.\n5. Prepare your produce: if it is the broccoli, cut it into florets; if it is the bell pepper, cut it into 1-inch strips; if it is the onion, cut it into wedges.\n6. Toss the tempeh and your produce on the lined pan with half the glaze and spread them out with space between pieces, so they roast and char instead of steaming.\n7. Roast 22 to 26 minutes, tossing once halfway, until the vegetables char at the edges and the tempeh is firm and browned.\n8. Cook the edamame from frozen in boiling water 4 to 5 minutes, drain it and salt it lightly.\n9. Divide the quinoa, the edamame, and the roasted tempeh and vegetables between the 4 containers, and drizzle the rest of the glaze over each, because the second coat is what makes it glossy and sticky.\n10. Keep the pumpkin seeds separate in a small bag per serving so they stay crunchy.\n11. Cool with the lids off until the steam stops, about 20 to 30 minutes, then seal, date each one, and refrigerate within 1 hour, because cooked grains spoil fast.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months. Freeze on the cook day any container not eaten by day 4, and thaw it in the fridge overnight.\n13. Reheat: microwave 2 minutes, or 4 minutes from frozen, stirring halfway. Scatter the pumpkin seeds and sliced scallion over the top after heating.",
