 "method": "No reheating needed, eat cold. If you prefer it warm, microwave the grain and beans 90 seconds, then add the tuna and vegetables cold.",
 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a small pot with a lid, a fine strainer, a knife, a can opener, a jar with a lid, 5 containers, 5 small tubs and 5 small bags.\n2. Cook your grain first so it can cool: if it is the bulgur, pour 1 1/2 cups of boiling water over each cup, cover, and let it stand 15 to 20 minutes, until tender, then fluff it; if it is the quinoa, rinse it well, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup, 15 minutes, until the water is absorbed, then fluff it. Spread it on a plate to cool, because warm grain goes gummy in a sealed container. Weigh it cooked.\n3. Prepare your protein: if it is the tuna, drain it well and flake it with a fork; if it is the white beans, drain and rinse them, because canned beans come cooked and only need the salt washed off.\n4. Dice your vegetables into 1/2-inch pieces. If it is the onion, soak it 10 minutes in cold water with a splash of vinegar to take the raw bite off.\n5. Make the dressing in the jar: the juice of 2 lemons, 1 tbsp mustard, 1 minced garlic clove, 1 tsp dried oregano, 1/2 tsp salt and pepper, shaken hard so the mustard pulls it together. If your fat is the olive oil, shake it in too.\n6. Divide the grain between the 5 containers, then your protein and the olives.\n7. If it is the bell pepper, add it to the containers now. If it is the onion, add it to the containers now. If it is the cucumber, pack it in a small bag per serving, because it makes everything watery by day three. If it is the tomato, pack it in a small bag per serving, because it makes everything watery by day three.\n8. Pour the dressing into the 5 small tubs and crumble the feta over each container.\n9. Once the grain is fully cool, seal the containers, date each one, and refrigerate them; nothing else here was hot.\n10. Storage: fridge 4 days. Do not freeze, because the cucumber and tomato turn watery and the feta goes grainy.\n11. To eat: cold. Shake the dressing and pour it over, add your vegetables from their bag if you packed them separately, and stir through chopped parsley or dill. For a warm bowl, microwave just the grain and your protein 90 seconds, until steaming hot (165F), and add the vegetables cold.",
