 "method": "Microwave one container 2 to 3 minutes, or reheat in a 375F oven 12 minutes to firm the top back up.",
 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large skillet, a large pot, a colander, a masher, a 9x13 baking dish, a knife and 5 containers. Heat the oven to 400F.\n2. Cook the lentils: rinse them and simmer them in 3 cups of water per cup, 18 to 25 minutes, until tender but holding their shape, then drain them. Weigh them cooked.\n3. Peel the sweet potatoes, cut them into 1-inch chunks, and boil them in salted water 15 to 18 minutes, until a fork slides in easily. Drain them and let them steam dry 2 minutes, because wet potatoes make a watery mash.\n4. Mash them with 1/4 cup of broth, 1/2 tsp salt, pepper and a pinch of nutmeg until smooth. If your fat is the olive oil, mash 1 tbsp of it in.\n5. If it is the onion, dice it small. If it is the carrots, dice them small. Mince 3 garlic cloves.\n6. Mist the skillet with cooking spray over medium-high and cook your produce with the garlic 5 to 6 minutes, until softened and browning, because browning builds the savory depth this dish relies on.\n7. Stir in the lentils, 1 tbsp tomato paste, 1 cup of broth, 2 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tsp dried thyme, 1 tsp smoked paprika and 1 tbsp vinegar, and simmer 5 to 8 minutes, until thick enough to hold a line behind the spoon, because a wet filling makes the topping slide off.\n8. Stir in the green peas straight from frozen, then spread the filling in the baking dish.\n9. Spread the mash over the top and rough up the surface with a fork, because the ridges crisp. Bake 18 to 20 minutes, until the top is set and golden at the edges.\n10. Cool the dish 20 minutes uncovered, because the filling firms as it cools and cuts cleanly, then cut it into 5 portions and lift them into the containers.\n11. Keep the pumpkin seeds separate in a small bag per serving so they stay crunchy. Seal the containers once they stop steaming, date each one, and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months. Freeze on the cook day any container not eaten by day 4, and thaw it in the fridge overnight.\n13. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes, or 375F oven 12 minutes to firm the top back up; from frozen, microwave 5 to 6 minutes. Sprinkle the pumpkin seeds and chopped parsley on top after heating.",
 "makes": 5,
 "season": "Tomato or garlic. Salt and black pepper through the lentils, and a splash of vinegar or Worcestershire for savoury depth.",
 "note": "Fully vegan (lentils, zucchini, sweet potato; soy sauce). Honest across all 5 tags.",
