 "method": "Microwave one container 2 minutes with a splash of water, stir, then drizzle ranch and add fresh celery and carrot sticks after heating.",
 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: two sheet pans, parchment, a knife, a large bowl, paper towels, a meat thermometer, 5 containers and 5 small bags. Heat the oven to 425F.\n2. Peel the sweet potatoes, cut them into 3/4-inch cubes, toss them with a little oil, 1/2 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp garlic powder, and spread them on one pan in a single layer, because crowded cubes steam instead of roasting.\n3. Prepare your produce: if it is the broccoli, cut it into florets and spread it beside the sweet potato to roast; if it is the carrots, cut them into sticks and pack them raw in a small bag per serving; if it is the celery, cut it into sticks and pack them raw in a small bag per serving.\n4. Pat the chicken breasts dry, because a dry surface browns, cut them into 1-inch pieces, toss them with a little oil, 1/2 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, and spread them on the second pan.\n5. Roast both pans 20 to 24 minutes, until the sweet potato edges caramelize and the chicken reads 165F in the thickest piece. Rest the chicken 5 minutes.\n6. Make the buffalo sauce in the bowl: whisk 1/3 cup hot sauce, 1 tsp honey, 1/2 tsp garlic powder and 1 tbsp water; the honey softens the vinegar bite and helps it cling.\n7. Add the hot chicken and toss to coat while it is hot, so the sauce soaks in instead of sliding off.\n8. Divide the sweet potato and the buffalo chicken between the 5 containers. If it is the broccoli, pack it alongside. If your fat is the cheddar, scatter it over each container now.\n9. Keep the avocado and the Greek yogurt ranch separate, because cut avocado browns and the ranch goes on after reheating so it stays cool.\n10. Cool with the lids off until the steam stops, about 20 minutes, then seal, date, and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n11. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months; freeze on the cook day any container not eaten by day 4.\n12. Reheat: microwave 2 minutes with a splash of water, or air fryer at 380F 5 minutes to crisp the potato; from frozen, microwave 4 to 5 minutes. After heating, drizzle on the ranch, add the avocado, and eat any raw sticks on the side.",
