 "method": "Microwave one container 2 to 3 minutes, or reheat in a 375F oven 12 minutes for a firmer texture. Add fresh avocado and salsa after heating.",
 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large skillet with a lid, a small pot, a 9x13 baking dish, a knife, a can opener and 5 containers. Heat the oven to 400F.\n2. Make the red enchilada sauce (or use 2 cups of jarred sauce): whisk 2 tbsp chili powder, 1 tsp ground cumin, 1 tsp dried oregano, 1/2 tsp garlic powder and 1/2 tsp salt into 2 cups of broth, simmer 10 minutes, until it coats a spoon, and stir in 1 tbsp vinegar.\n3. Cook your carb: if it is the sweet potato, peel it, cut it into 1/2-inch cubes, and cook it covered in the skillet with 1/4 cup of water over medium 10 to 12 minutes, until tender; if it is the tortillas, tear them into pieces and toast them on a sheet pan at 400F 5 to 6 minutes, until crisp, so they do not turn to mush under the sauce.\n4. If it is the bell pepper, dice it into 1/2-inch pieces. If it is the onion, dice it into 1/2-inch pieces. If it is the sweet corn, boil it from frozen 3 minutes and drain it.\n5. Add a little oil to the skillet over medium-high, bloom 1 tsp ground cumin and 1 tsp smoked paprika 30 seconds, then cook your produce 5 to 6 minutes, until soft.\n6. Drain and rinse the black beans, which come cooked, and stir them in with 1 tsp salt and the juice of 1 lime; cook 2 minutes. If it is the sweet potato, stir it in too.\n7. Build the bake: spread 1/2 cup of sauce in the dish, then layer half the filling, half the remaining sauce, then the rest of both. If it is the tortillas, lay half the pieces on the bottom and the rest in the middle. If your fat is the cheddar, scatter it on top, because it melts into a crust.\n8. Bake 22 to 25 minutes, until the edges bubble and the top browns.\n9. Cool the bake 25 minutes uncovered so it firms and cuts cleanly, then cut it into 5 portions and lift them into the containers.\n10. Keep the avocado and the salsa separate, because cut avocado browns.\n11. Seal the containers once they stop steaming, date them, and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months; freeze on the cook day any container not eaten by day 4.\n13. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes, or 375F oven 12 minutes for a crisper top; from frozen, microwave 5 to 6 minutes. Add the avocado, salsa and cilantro after heating.",
