 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large sheet pan, parchment, a medium pot with a lid, a large bowl, a knife, a meat thermometer and 5 containers. Heat the oven to 425F.\n2. Cook the brown rice first, because it takes the longest: simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup with a pinch of salt, 40 to 45 minutes, until the water is absorbed, then spread it on a tray to cool. Weigh it cooked.\n3. Make the teriyaki glaze in the bowl: whisk 1/3 cup soy sauce, 2 tbsp honey, 1 tbsp rice vinegar, 3 minced garlic cloves and 1 tsp grated ginger. If your fat is the sesame oil, whisk 1 tbsp of it in. Set aside 3 tbsp of the glaze for the end.\n4. Pat the chicken thighs dry, because a dry surface lets the glaze caramelize instead of steam, cut them into 1-inch pieces, and toss them in the bowl with the glaze.\n5. Trim the snap peas. Prepare your produce: if it is the broccoli, cut it into florets; if it is the bell pepper, cut it into strips; if it is the pineapple, cut it into 3/4-inch chunks, because its sugars caramelize at this heat.\n6. Spread the chicken on one half of the lined pan and your produce on the other, with space between the pieces so everything roasts instead of steaming.\n7. Roast 22 to 26 minutes, tossing once halfway, until the edges char and the thickest piece of chicken reads 165F.\n8. Scatter the snap peas over the pan for the last 5 minutes, so they stay crisp and bright green.\n9. Rest the chicken 5 minutes, then toss everything with the reserved glaze while it is hot, so it clings.\n10. Divide the rice, the chicken, the roasted produce and the snap peas between the 5 containers. Keep the cashews separate in a small bag per serving so they stay crunchy.\n11. Cool with the lids off until the steam stops, about 20 minutes, then seal, date, and refrigerate within 1 hour, because cooked rice spoils fast.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months; freeze on the cook day any container not eaten by day 4.\n13. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes with a splash of water, stirring halfway, or 4 to 5 minutes from frozen. Scatter the cashews, a sprinkle of sesame seeds and sliced scallion on top after heating so the nuts stay crunchy.",
