 "method": "Scoop bulgur into a bowl, add a portion of lentils and the roasted vegetables, and stir in a handful of spinach while warm. Drizzle the lemon-tahini sauce over the top.",
 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large sheet pan, parchment, 2 small pots with lids, a small bowl and a whisk for the sauce, a cutting board, a knife and 5 containers. Heat the oven to 425F.\n2. Cut your vegetables into 1/2-inch pieces, toss them on the lined sheet pan with the olive oil, 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp ground coriander and 1 tsp salt, and spread them in one layer, because crowded pieces steam instead of browning.\n3. Roast the vegetables 22 to 25 minutes, stirring once, until the edges brown and a fork slides through. If your vegetables are the spinach, skip the oven and keep it raw for the end, because it wilts in seconds.\n4. While they roast, cook the lentils: rinse them and simmer them in 3 cups of water per cup, 18 to 25 minutes, until tender but still holding their shape. Drain them and salt them while warm, because lentils only take on salt while they are hot.\n5. Cook the bulgur in the second pot: 2 cups of water per cup with 1/2 tsp salt, covered, at a low simmer 12 to 15 minutes, until the water is absorbed and the grains are tender. Fluff it and weigh it cooked.\n6. Make the sauce: whisk your fat with the juice of 1 lemon, 1 minced garlic clove, 1/2 tsp cumin and 1/2 tsp salt, then whisk in warm water a spoon at a time until it pours easily. It can look grainy before it turns smooth, so keep whisking.\n7. Divide the bulgur between the 5 containers, then top each with a fifth of the lentils and your vegetables, and tuck a small handful of the spinach on top of each.\n8. Pour the sauce into 5 small lidded cups, one per container, because it soaks into the bulgur if it sits on the bowls for days.\n9. Cool the containers with the lids off until they stop steaming, then seal, write the date on each and refrigerate within 1 hour, because cooked grains spoil faster than most foods.\n10. Storage: fridge 4 days for the bowls and 5 for the sauce, freezer 2 months for the bowls without the sauce.\n11. Reheat: microwave a bowl 2 minutes with a splash of water, until hot and the spinach wilts, then drizzle the sauce over after heating and finish with chopped parsley and a pinch of sumac.",
 "makes": 5,
 "season": "Tahini or Lemon or garlic or Cumin (ground) or olive oil. Salt to taste as the lentils warm; undersalted lentils taste like nothing.",
 "note": "Vegan and fiber-rich; sauce kept separate to drizzle after reheating.",
