 "method": "Add a portion of the buffalo chicken, roasted potatoes, and broccoli to a bowl. Top with a handful of chopped romaine, carrot, and celery for crunch, and drizzle the Greek yogurt ranch over the top.",
 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: 2 large sheet pans, parchment, a cutting board, a knife, a meat thermometer, a large bowl, paper towels and 5 containers. Heat the oven to 425F.\n2. Cut the potatoes into 3/4-inch cubes, skin on, toss them on one lined sheet pan with the olive oil, 1/2 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp garlic powder, and spread them in one layer, because crowded cubes steam instead of browning.\n3. Roast the potatoes 25 to 30 minutes, stirring once, until golden and a fork slides in easily.\n4. While they roast, pat the chicken breast dry and cut it into 1-inch pieces, because a dry surface browns and a wet one steams.\n5. Spread the chicken on the second lined pan with a light mist of cooking spray, 1/2 tsp salt and black pepper, and roast it 15 to 18 minutes, until the thickest piece reads 165F. Rest it 5 minutes so the juices settle back into the meat.\n6. Cut the carrots into sticks and keep them raw in a bag per container, because they are the crunch on top. If your vegetables are the broccoli, cut it into florets and roast it beside the chicken for the same 15 to 18 minutes, until the edges char. If your vegetables are the celery, cut it into sticks and keep it raw with the carrots. If your vegetables are the romaine, chop it and keep it raw in a bag so it stays crisp.\n7. Whisk 1/3 cup hot sauce, the butter melted, 1 tsp honey and 1 minced garlic clove in the large bowl, because the butter and honey tame the vinegar bite and help the sauce cling. Toss the rested chicken in it.\n8. Divide the potatoes and any roasted vegetables between the 5 containers, then top each with a fifth of the buffalo chicken.\n9. Keep the carrots, any raw vegetables and your fat in separate small containers, one per serving, and add them after heating, because ranch and cheese go greasy in the microwave.\n10. Cool the containers with the lids off until they stop steaming, about 20 minutes, then seal, write the date on each and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n11. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months for the chicken and potatoes only.\n12. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes until hot, or air-fry at 380F for 6 minutes to crisp the potatoes. Top with the carrots, your raw vegetables and your fat after heating.",
 "makes": 5,
 "season": "Extra hot sauce or a pinch of garlic powder.",
 "note": "Spicy batch chicken; crunchy salad and ranch added fresh after reheating.",
