  "method": "Ladle a portion of chili into a bowl and heat through. Top with a little shredded cheddar and a few cubes of avocado just before eating.",
  "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large heavy pot, a cutting board, a knife, a colander, a ladle, a meat thermometer and 5 containers.\n2. Dice your vegetables into 1/2-inch pieces, plus 1 onion and 3 garlic cloves for the base.\n3. If it is the ground turkey, add a little oil to the pot over medium-high, add the turkey, let it sit 2 minutes so a brown crust forms, then break it up and cook 5 to 6 minutes more, until no pink remains and it reads 165F. If it is the kidney beans, drain and rinse them. If it is the black beans, drain and rinse them.\n4. If it is the pinto beans, drain and rinse them. If it is the sweet potato, peel it and cut it into 1/2-inch cubes so it cooks through in the simmer.\n5. Add the onion, garlic and your vegetables to the pot with 1/4 cup broth and cook over medium 5 minutes, until soft, scraping up any browned bits, because they carry the flavor.\n6. Stir in 2 tbsp tomato paste, 1 to 2 chopped chipotles in adobo, 1 tbsp cumin, 2 tsp chili powder, 1 tsp smoked paprika and 1 tsp dried oregano, and cook 1 to 2 minutes, until the paste darkens, so the spices toast instead of tasting dusty.\n7. Stir your carb and any drained beans into the pot with 3 cups broth and 1 tsp salt, bring it to a boil, then lower it to a simmer and cook uncovered 25 to 30 minutes, stirring now and then, until it thickens. If your carb is the sweet potato, it is done when a fork slides through a cube.\n8. Off the heat, stir in the juice of 1 lime and a handful of chopped cilantro, because acid lifts a long-simmered pot.\n9. Ladle the chili evenly into the 5 containers straight away, because a full pot cools too slowly to be safe.\n10. Cool the containers with the lids off until they stop steaming, then seal, write the date on each and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n11. Keep the avocado out of the containers and dice it when you eat, because cut avocado browns. Keep the cheddar out of the containers and add it after reheating, because reheated cheese goes rubbery.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months without the toppings.\n13. Reheat: microwave 3 to 4 minutes, stirring halfway, until steaming. From frozen, thaw overnight in the fridge first. Top with the cheddar and diced avocado.",
