  "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a mixing bowl, a fine strainer, a small pot with a lid, a small lidded jar for the dressing, a cutting board, a knife and 4 containers (divided boxes work best).\n2. Prepare your carb. If it is the quinoa, rinse it, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup with a pinch of salt, 15 to 18 minutes, until the water is absorbed, then fluff it, spread it on a plate to cool, and weigh it cooked. If it is the pita, cut each one into wedges and keep them in a paper towel so they stay soft.\n3. Make the dressing in the jar: the juice of 1 lemon, 2 tbsp olive oil, 1 tsp mustard, 1 small grated garlic clove, 1/2 tsp dried oregano, 1/2 tsp salt and black pepper, shaken hard for 20 seconds.\n4. Prepare your protein. If it is the canned tuna, drain it well and press it in the strainer so the box does not turn watery, and it needs no heat because it is already cooked well past 145F in the can. If it is the white beans, drain and rinse them until the foam stops, no cooking needed, and shake them dry.\n5. Toss your protein in the bowl with half the dressing and 2 tbsp finely diced onion, folding gently so nothing gets mashed, and let it sit 5 minutes so it drinks up the dressing.\n6. Cut your vegetables into bite-size pieces and pat them dry. If your vegetables are the tomato, keep the wedges in their own corner of the box, because their juice soaks everything else. If your vegetables are the arugula, keep it whole and dry in its own section so it stays crisp.\n7. Fill each container with a quarter of the protein salad in the largest section and your vegetables and your carb in the others, then top the salad with your fat, the olives and the feta.\n8. Pour the rest of the dressing into 4 tiny lidded cups, one per box, because dressed vegetables go limp within an hour.\n9. Everything is already cool, so seal the boxes, write the date on each and refrigerate straight away.\n10. Storage: fridge 3 days. Do not freeze, because raw vegetables and feta go watery when they thaw.\n11. To eat: cold, no reheating. Drizzle the saved dressing over the vegetables, pile the salad onto them, and scoop it up with your carb.",
