 "method": "Cut one square and microwave 60 to 75 seconds until hot, or reheat in an air fryer at 350F for 4 minutes for crisp edges.",
 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a rimmed sheet pan or 9x13 baking dish, parchment, a large bowl, a whisk, a cutting board, a knife and 5 containers. Heat the oven to 425F, because high heat browns the potatoes instead of steaming them.\n2. Cut the potatoes into 1/2-inch cubes, skin on, and dice your vegetables.\n3. Toss the potatoes with the olive oil, 1/2 tsp salt, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika and 1/4 tsp black pepper on the lined pan, in one layer with space between the cubes, because piled cubes steam and stay pale.\n4. Roast the potatoes 18 minutes, then add your vegetables to the pan and roast 7 minutes more, until the potato edges are golden and a fork slides through. If your vegetables are the spinach, skip the second roast and scatter the leaves over the pan just before the eggs go on, because they wilt in seconds.\n5. While the pan roasts, whisk your protein with 1/2 tsp salt, 1/4 tsp black pepper and 1/2 tsp garlic powder for 30 seconds, until even in color. If your protein is the cheddar, shred it instead and skip the whisk.\n6. Lower the oven to 375F, pour the mix evenly over the whole pan, and sprinkle the cheddar on top.\n7. Bake 16 to 20 minutes, until the eggs are set, puffed, no longer jiggle in the center and read 160F.\n8. Cool the pan 10 minutes so the slab firms up and cuts clean, then cut it into 5 equal squares.\n9. Put one square in each of the 5 containers, lids off until they stop steaming, then seal, write the date on each and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n10. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months wrapped tightly.\n11. Reheat: microwave one square 60 to 75 seconds with a splash of water, or air-fry at 350F 4 minutes to bring back the crisp potato edges. A few dashes of hot sauce on top.",
 "makes": 5,
