  "method": "Unwrap, wrap loosely in a paper towel, and microwave 90 seconds to 2 minutes from frozen until steaming. Top with salsa.",
  "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large skillet, a bowl, a whisk, a meat thermometer, 5 foil squares, and a freezer zip bag or 5 containers.\n2. Dice your vegetables into small pieces, because big pieces tear the tortilla when you roll.\n3. Drain and rinse the black beans.\n4. Prepare your protein. If it is the ground turkey, cook it in the skillet with a little oil over medium-high, 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up, until no pink remains and it reads 165F, then tip it into the bowl. If it is the eggs or egg whites, whisk them in the bowl, pour them into the skillet with a little oil over medium-low, and push them gently around 3 to 4 minutes until just set and no longer wet (160F), pulling them off a touch soft so they stay tender when you warm them later, then tip them back into the bowl. If it is the black beans, warm them in the skillet 2 minutes, then tip them into the bowl. If it is the cheddar, shred it and keep it for the roll.\n5. Cook your vegetables in the skillet with a little oil over medium, 3 minutes, until soft.\n6. Sprinkle in 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp chili powder, 1/2 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp garlic powder and stir 30 seconds, so the spices toast and taste deep instead of dusty.\n7. Stir in the black beans and cook 2 minutes, until hot, then scrape everything into the bowl with your protein.\n8. Let the filling cool to warm, about 10 minutes, because hot filling steams the tortilla and makes it soggy.\n9. Warm the tortillas 20 seconds in the microwave so they fold without cracking.\n10. Lay a tortilla flat, add a fifth of the filling in a line, sprinkle on the cheddar, fold in the sides and roll it tight. Repeat for all 5.\n11. Wrap each burrito snugly in foil, write the date on it, and get them into the fridge or freezer within 2 hours.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, or freezer 2 months in the zip bag.\n13. Reheat: unwrap, wrap loosely in a paper towel, and microwave 90 seconds to 2 minutes from frozen, flipping halfway, until steaming through, or 60 to 75 seconds from the fridge. Finish 2 minutes in a dry skillet for crisp edges. Top with the salsa.",
