  "method": "Unwrap, wrap loosely in a paper towel, microwave 90 seconds to 2 minutes from frozen until steaming. Top with salsa.",
  "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large skillet with a lid, a clean kitchen towel, a cutting board, a knife, 5 foil squares, a freezer zip bag and 5 containers.\n2. Drain and rinse the black beans.\n3. Prepare your protein. If it is the tofu, drain it, wrap it in the towel and press it hard for 1 minute, because dry tofu browns instead of stewing, then crumble it into pea-size pieces. If it is the black beans, crush about a third of them with a fork so the filling holds together.\n4. Dice your vegetables into small pieces. If your carb is the sweet potato, cut it into 1/2-inch cubes, cook it in the skillet over medium with a little oil and the lid on, 8 to 10 minutes, until a fork slides through, then set it aside.\n5. Add a little oil to the skillet over medium, add your vegetables and cook 3 minutes, until soft.\n6. Push the vegetables aside, add your protein to the bare pan and cook 5 minutes, stirring now and then, until it firms up and any liquid cooks off.\n7. Sprinkle in 1 tsp turmeric, 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp chili powder, the nutritional yeast, 3/4 tsp salt and 1/4 tsp black pepper and stir 30 seconds, so the spices toast instead of tasting dusty.\n8. Stir in the black beans and cook 2 minutes, until hot, then taste and add salt if it is flat. If your carb is the sweet potato, fold it in now.\n9. Let the filling cool to warm, about 10 minutes, because hot filling steams and turns soggy.\n10. If your carb is the tortillas, warm them 20 seconds in the microwave so they fold without cracking, then lay one flat, add a fifth of the filling in a line, fold in the sides, roll it tight and wrap it snugly in foil. If your carb is the sweet potato, divide the filling between the 5 containers instead and seal them once they stop steaming.\n11. Write the date on each and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months in the zip bag.\n13. Reheat: microwave 90 seconds to 2 minutes from frozen, wrapped loosely in a paper towel, flipping halfway, until steaming, or 60 to 75 seconds from the fridge. Top with the salsa and a squeeze of lime. If your fat is the raw avocado, dice it fresh on top, because it browns if cut ahead.",
