  "method": "Microwave one square 45 to 60 seconds with a splash of milk, or eat cold. Top with extra berries.",
  "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: an 8x8 or 9x9 baking dish, parchment, 2 bowls, a whisk, a cooling rack and 5 containers. Heat the oven to 350F.\n2. Line the dish with parchment, leaving overhang on two sides, so you can lift the whole slab out later.\n3. Stir the oats, 1 1/2 tsp baking powder, 1 1/2 tsp cinnamon, 1/4 tsp nutmeg and 1/4 tsp salt together in one bowl, so the baking powder and spice spread evenly and every square rises and tastes the same.\n4. Whisk your protein in the second bowl with the maple syrup and 1 tsp vanilla, then add unsweetened almond milk until the mix is loose and pourable, about 1 cup. If your fruit is the banana, mash it and whisk it in, because it adds moisture and sweetness. If your fruit is the blueberries, keep them whole to fold in at the end.\n5. Pour the wet mix into the dry and stir just until everything is moistened, because overmixing makes the squares gummy. Fold in the walnuts, chopped, and any whole fruit.\n6. Pour the batter into the lined dish, spread it level and scatter a few extra walnut pieces on top.\n7. Bake 30 to 35 minutes, until the top is golden and set, a knife in the center comes out clean and the middle reads 160F.\n8. Cool the slab in the dish 20 minutes, because it firms up as it cools and then cuts into clean squares, then lift it out by the parchment and cut it into 5 equal squares.\n9. Put one square in each of the 5 containers, lids off until they stop steaming, then seal, write the date on each and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n10. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 2 months.\n11. Reheat: microwave one square 45 to 60 seconds with a splash of milk, or eat it cold. Top with your fruit and a thin drizzle of the maple syrup.",
