 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: 5 pint jars with lids as your 5 containers, a bowl, a spoon and 5 small zip bags or lidded cups for the granola.\n2. Stir your protein in the bowl with 2 tsp vanilla, 1 tsp cinnamon, the honey and a tiny pinch of salt until smooth, because the salt and vanilla are what make it taste like dessert instead of plain curds. If it is the oats, stir them in too, so they soften overnight.\n3. If it is the chia seeds, stir them into the bowl, wait 5 minutes and stir again, because chia thickens the mix and clumps if left alone. If it is the almonds, chop them and keep them with the granola so they stay crunchy.\n4. Portion the granola into the 5 small bags, one per jar, because granola sitting on anything wet goes soft within hours.\n5. Divide the mix between the 5 jars and seal the lids.\n6. Keep your fruit in a small tub per jar, because cut fruit weeps juice into the jar by day two.\n7. Everything is cool already, so refrigerate the jars straight away and keep the granola bags at room temperature.\n8. Storage: fridge 4 days. Do not freeze, because the base turns grainy and watery when it thaws.\n9. To eat: cold. Stir the jar if a little liquid has separated, then tip your fruit on top, and the granola last so every bite has crunch. If the jar is too full for it, tip the jar into a bowl first.",
