  "method": "Grab 2 to 3 balls (one portion) from the fridge and eat cold. No reheating needed. If they feel too firm straight from the fridge, let them sit on the counter 5 minutes to soften.",
  "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large mixing bowl, a sturdy spoon or spatula, a spoon for scooping, a plate or small sheet pan that fits in the fridge, and 5 containers.\n2. Tip the oats, your protein, the chia seeds, 1/2 tsp cinnamon and a pinch of salt into the bowl and stir them together first, so the powder spreads evenly instead of clumping in pockets.\n3. Add the peanut butter and the honey and stir hard until everything pulls together into one thick, sticky dough.\n4. Press a spoonful of the dough: it should hold its shape. The powders drink up liquid, so it usually needs several spoonfuls of water: work them in one at a time, then let the dough sit 5 minutes so the oats and chia soak them up. If it is too sticky to roll, rest it in the fridge 10 minutes, because cold peanut butter firms up.\n5. Fold in the dark chocolate chips last, so they stay whole instead of smearing through the dough.\n6. Roll the dough into balls about 1 inch wide with damp hands, which keeps it from sticking to your palms, and set them on the plate.\n7. Chill the balls uncovered 30 minutes so they firm up and hold together.\n8. Divide the balls between the 5 containers, the same number in each, and seal them. They are already cool, so they go straight into the fridge.\n9. Storage: fridge 7 days, or freezer 2 months in a single layer in a bag.\n10. To eat: cold, straight from the fridge, no reheating; from frozen, leave them on the counter 15 minutes to soften.",
