  "season": "Per block of tofu: 1/2 tsp turmeric (for color), 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp onion powder, 3/4 tsp salt, black pepper, and 1 tsp nutritional yeast for a savory, eggy depth. A squeeze of hot sauce at the end.",
  "method": "1. Dice the potato into 1/2-inch cubes.\n2. Heat the olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat, add the potato and a pinch of salt, and cook covered 5 minutes, then uncovered 8 to 10 minutes more, stirring now and then, until golden and tender when poked with a fork. Weigh it cooked.\n3. While the potato cooks, press the tofu between paper towels for 5 minutes, then crumble it into small pieces, because dry tofu browns instead of steaming.\n4. Mix the seasonings in a small bowl: 1/4 tsp turmeric for color, 1/4 tsp garlic powder, 1/4 tsp onion powder, 1/2 tsp salt, black pepper and 1 tsp nutritional yeast for savory depth.\n5. Push the potato to one side, add the tofu and the seasonings to the pan, and cook 6 to 8 minutes, stirring now and then, until the tofu is golden with dry edges.\n6. Fold in the spinach and cook 1 to 2 minutes, until wilted.\n7. Serve hot with a few dashes of hot sauce over the top.",
  "note": "Turmeric makes it look like eggs; nutritional yeast and garlic/onion powder give the savory, eggy flavor tofu lacks. Patting dry is what lets it brown.",
