 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large pot with a lid, a colander, a cutting board, a knife, a ladle, a meat thermometer and 5 containers.\n2. Cook your protein first. If it is the ground turkey, brown the ground turkey in the olive oil over medium-high, breaking it up, 6 to 8 minutes, until no pink remains and it reads 165F, then lift it out. If it is the turkey breast, cut the turkey breast into 3/4-inch cubes, brown them in the olive oil over medium-high, 2 to 3 minutes a side, and lift them out, because they finish cooking in the soup and must read 165F before you eat.\n3. Dice the onion, mince the garlic and chop the tomato.\n4. Add the onion and the garlic to the pot and cook over medium 4 to 5 minutes, until soft, scraping up the browned bits, which are flavor. If it is the carrots, dice them and cook them with the onion so they soften. If it is the celery, slice it and cook it with the onion.\n5. Add the tomato, the broth, 3 cups of water, 1 tsp dried rosemary, a pinch of chili flakes and 1/2 tsp salt, and bring it to a simmer.\n6. Drain and rinse your beans in the colander, because the liquid in the can makes the soup cloudy and salty, then stir them into the pot with the meat and bring it back to a simmer.\n7. Simmer, lid on a crack, 15 minutes, until the vegetables are tender and the meat is hot through. If it is the kale, strip the leaves off the stems, tear them into pieces, and stir them in for the last 5 minutes so they soften but keep their color.\n8. Take it off the heat, squeeze in the juice of half a lemon, and taste for salt. The lemon is what stops a bean soup tasting flat.\n9. Ladle the soup into the 5 containers straight away, because a full pot cools too slowly.\n10. Cool the containers with the lids off until they stop steaming, then seal, write the date on each, and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n11. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months.\n12. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes, stirring halfway, or warm it on the stove, with a splash of water if the beans have soaked up the broth. Finish with black pepper and more lemon.",
