 "method": "1. Soften the onion, pepper and garlic in the oil for 6 minutes. 2. Add the tomato, beans and broth and simmer 12 minutes. 3. Nestle the fish in the stew, cover, and cook 6 to 8 minutes until it flakes. 4. Stir in the spinach.",
 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a wide pan with a lid, a small pan for the fish, a cutting board, a knife, a meat thermometer, 4 freezer bags and 4 containers.\n2. Dice the onion and mince the garlic.\n3. Warm the olive oil in the wide pan over medium, add the onion and the garlic, and cook 6 to 8 minutes, stirring, until soft and sweet. If it is the bell pepper, dice it and cook it with the onion so it softens.\n4. Stir in 1 tsp smoked paprika and a pinch of chili flakes and cook 30 seconds, until fragrant, so the spices bloom in the oil.\n5. Add the broth, 1 cup of water and 1/2 tsp salt and bring it to a simmer. If it is the tomato, chop the tomato and add it now so it breaks down into the base. If it is the white beans, drain and rinse the white beans and add them now. If it is the potato, cut the potato into 3/4-inch cubes and add it now, because it needs the full simmer to turn tender.\n6. Simmer the base, lid off, 15 to 18 minutes, until it has thickened a little and everything in it is tender. Add the juice of half a lemon and taste for salt. If it is the spinach, stir it into the hot base so it just wilts.\n7. Divide the base between the 4 containers straight away, because a full pan cools too slowly. The fish stays out: cooked fish fades after 2 to 3 days, so it is cooked fresh in each portion on the day.\n8. Portion your protein raw into the 4 freezer bags and freeze them today, because raw fish keeps only 1 to 2 days uncooked in the fridge. Move one bag to the fridge the night before you want it.\n9. Cool the containers with the lids off until they stop steaming, then seal, write the date on each, and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n10. Storage: fridge 4 days for the base, freezer 2 months for the base, and up to 3 months for the raw fish in its bags.\n11. To cook on the day: bring one portion of the base to a simmer in the small pan, nestle your protein in, cover, and cook over medium-low 6 to 8 minutes, until it reads 145F and flakes easily.\n12. Reheat: the base heats through while the fish cooks, so there is nothing else to warm. Finish with parsley, black pepper and more lemon.",
