 "method": "1. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice for 40 to 45 minutes until tender, rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked. If it is the white rice, rinse it, simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice for 15 to 18 minutes until the water is absorbed, rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked.\n2. Heat 2 cups of water in a pot to a bare simmer, with small bubbles at the edge and no rolling boil.\n3. Cut the tofu into cubes and add it with the edamame. Warm them 3 to 4 minutes, until the edamame is hot all the way through, and handle the tofu gently so it keeps its shape.\n4. Stir in your greens and cook 1 to 2 minutes, until wilted.\n5. Take the pot off the heat. Whisk the miso with a ladle of the hot water in a small bowl until smooth, then stir it back in. Do not let it boil again, because heat kills the live cultures and flattens the flavor.\n6. Spoon your grain into a bowl, ladle the soup over it and top with 1 sliced scallion, a splash of soy sauce and a few drops of the sesame oil.",
 "season": "The miso is the salt. Never boil it once it is in or you kill the live cultures and flatten the flavour. Sliced scallion and a little soy sauce.",
 "note": "Miso is fermented soybean with live cultures, and tofu plus edamame makes this a proper protein bowl."
