 "method": "1. Simmer the broth with the onion, carrot and zucchini for 10 minutes. 2. Add the rice and shredded chicken. 3. Serve with the avocado and a lot of lime.",
 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large pot with a lid (6 to 8 quarts), a small pot for the grain, a cutting board, a knife, a ladle, a meat thermometer and 5 containers.\n2. Cook your protein first so it can rest while the soup simmers: pat it dry, season it with salt, pepper and 1 tsp ground cumin, and cook it in a hot pan with a light mist of cooking spray over medium-high, 5 to 7 minutes a side, until it reads 165F in the thickest part. Rest it 5 minutes so the juices settle back into the meat, then shred it with two forks.\n3. Cook your grain in the small pot: rinse it, then simmer it covered in salted water until tender and the water is absorbed (white rice takes about 18 minutes in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup; brown rice 40 to 45 minutes in 2 cups per cup). Rest it 5 minutes off the heat and fluff it. Weigh it cooked.\n4. Dice the onion and your vegetables into even 1/2-inch pieces so they cook at the same rate.\n5. Bring the broth to a simmer in the large pot with the onion, 1 tsp dried oregano and a pinch of salt. Add your vegetables and simmer 8 to 10 minutes, until just tender; they soften a little more every time you reheat.\n6. Stir the shredded meat and the cooked grain into the pot and simmer 2 minutes, just to heat through. Taste it and add salt if it is flat.\n7. Ladle the soup evenly into the 5 containers straight away: a full pot cools too slowly and sits for hours in the 40 to 140F range where bacteria grow fastest.\n8. Cool the containers with the lids off until they stop steaming, about 20 to 30 minutes, then seal them, write the date on each, and get them in the fridge within 2 hours of cooking.\n9. Keep the avocado and the lime out of the containers: cut avocado browns, and lime juice turns the grain mushy overnight.\n10. Storage: fridge 4 days, or freezer 3 months without the avocado.\n11. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes, stirring halfway, or warm it on the stove, with a splash of water if the grain has soaked up the broth. Add the diced avocado, a big squeeze of lime, cilantro, chili flakes and a little jalapeno to the bowl.",
