 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a medium pot, a colander, a sheet pan or tray, a large bowl, a small bowl for the dressing, a cutting board, a knife and 4 containers.\n2. Cut the potato into 1-inch chunks and boil it in salted water 12 to 15 minutes, until a knife slides in with no resistance. If it is the green beans, trim them and drop them into the same pot for the last 4 minutes so they come out bright green and just tender.\n3. Drain everything and spread it on the tray to cool 15 minutes. Cooled potato is firmer, holds the dressing better, and carries resistant starch, which feeds your gut bacteria.\n4. Make the dressing in the small bowl: stir the yogurt with the juice of half a lemon, the chopped pickles, 2 tbsp chopped dill, 1/2 tsp salt and black pepper.\n5. Toss the cooled potato through the dressing with the olive oil. If it is the green beans, toss them in too. If it is the tomato, cut the tomato into wedges and fold them in gently so they do not break up. If it is the cucumber, cut the cucumber into thick half-moons and keep them in a separate small container, one portion per serving, because cucumber waters down the dressing within hours.\n6. Divide the salad between the 4 containers, then drain the sardines, break them into large pieces, and lay them on top, so they stay whole instead of mashing into the dressing.\n7. Everything is already cool, so seal the containers, write the date on each, and refrigerate.\n8. Storage: fridge 3 days. Do not freeze it, because the yogurt splits and the potato turns grainy.\n9. To eat: cold, straight from the container. If it is the cucumber, tip it in just before you eat. Finish with more dill, black pepper and a squeeze of lemon.",
