 "method": "1. If it is the brown rice, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice for 40 to 45 minutes until tender, rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked. If it is the quinoa, rinse it well so it does not taste bitter, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of quinoa for 12 to 15 minutes until the water is absorbed, rest it 5 minutes off the heat, fluff it with a fork and weigh it cooked.\n2. Heat the oven to 400F.\n3. Chop the almonds finely and mix them with 1 tsp lemon zest, a pinch of salt and some black pepper, so the crust is seasoned.\n4. Pat the trout dry, brush the top with the Dijon mustard and press the almond mix on top, because the mustard is what holds the crust on.\n5. Bake the trout 10 to 12 minutes, until the crust is golden and the fish flakes easily with a fork (145F).\n6. While the fish bakes, steam your vegetables covered over 1 inch of simmering water for 4 to 6 minutes, until bright green and tender with a little bite.\n7. Serve the trout with your grain and your vegetables, with a squeeze of lemon over everything.",
 "season": "Salt, black pepper, lemon zest in the almonds, and a squeeze of lemon over everything.",
 "note": "The mustard holds the almond crust on and seasons the fish at the same time."
