 "method": "1. Toast the rye bread 2 to 3 minutes, until crisp at the edges, then spread it thinly with the Dijon mustard.\n2. Beat your protein with a pinch of salt and a pinch of black pepper, because salting eggs before they cook keeps them tender.\n3. Warm your fat in a nonstick pan over low heat and pour in the beaten mix. Stir slowly 3 to 4 minutes, pulling the curds across the pan, until just set and creamy with no runny parts (160F).\n4. Pull the pan off the heat while the curds still look glossy, because they keep cooking in the hot pan.\n5. Pile the scramble on the rye bread and top with a sprinkle of chives and a forkful of your vegetables.",
