 "method": "1. Boil the egg: lower it into a pot of boiling water and cook it 10 to 12 minutes, until the yolk is firm (160F). Cool it in cold water so the shell slips off.\n2. If your protein is the Atlantic salmon, pat it dry, salt it lightly and sear it in a little oil over medium-high heat, skin side down if it has skin, 4 to 5 minutes, then flip it and cook 2 to 3 minutes more, until it flakes easily (145F). If your protein is the canned salmon, drain and rinse it and break it into big flakes, no cooking needed.\n3. Toast the rye bread 2 to 3 minutes, until crisp at the edges, then spread it with the skyr.\n4. Peel and slice the egg and slice your vegetables thin. Lay the egg on the skyr, then add your protein. Cover with your vegetables, then finish with the olive oil, a sprinkle of dill, a squeeze of lemon and a few capers.",
