 "method": "1. Stir the oats, the chia seeds, a pinch of salt and 1/2 tsp cinnamon together in a bowl.\n2. If your protein is kefir, pour it over the oats and stir until no dry oats are left. If your protein is the whey protein powder, whisk it with 1/2 cup of milk until smooth, then stir it into the oats.\n3. Cover the bowl and chill it in the fridge overnight, or at least 4 hours, so the oats soften and the chia seeds swell into a thick, creamy pudding. In a hurry, let it sit on the counter 30 minutes instead, though the oats stay chewier.\n4. In the morning, stir it well, loosen it with a splash of milk if it is too thick, and top with the chopped Brazil nuts and your fruit. Serve cold.",
