 "method": "1. Bring a wide pot of water to a gentle simmer and add a splash of vinegar, which helps the whites hold together around the yolk.\n2. While it heats, grate the garlic, stir it with a pinch of salt into the Greek yogurt and spread it across a plate.\n3. Crack the eggs one at a time into a cup and slide them into the water. Poach them 3 to 4 minutes, until the whites are set and the yolks are as firm as you like (160F for a firm yolk). Lift them out with a slotted spoon and blot them dry.\n4. Toast or warm your carb 1 to 2 minutes, until warm and lightly crisp, for dipping.\n5. Warm your fat with 1/2 tsp chili flakes in a small pan over medium-low heat 1 to 2 minutes, until it sizzles and turns red, then pull it off the heat before the chili burns.\n6. Set the eggs on the yogurt and spoon the sizzling fat over the top. Add a sprinkle of dill and a squeeze of lemon, and serve with your vegetables on the side and your carb for dipping.",
