 "method": "1. Cook the lentils: rinse them and simmer them in 3 cups of water per cup of lentils, 18 to 25 minutes, until tender, then drain them (canned lentils only need draining and rinsing). Weigh them cooked.\n2. While they simmer, heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add the diced onion and the garlic and cook 4 to 5 minutes, until soft and golden, because slow-cooked onion gives the dish its sweetness.\n3. Stir in 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika and a pinch of chili flakes, and cook 30 seconds, until fragrant, so the spices bloom in the oil.\n4. Add the drained lentils with a splash of water and warm them through 3 to 5 minutes, stirring now and then, until hot.\n5. Stir your vegetables in next. If your vegetables are the tomato, dice it and cook it 2 to 3 minutes, until it softens. If your vegetables are the spinach, cook it 30 to 60 seconds, until wilted.\n6. Spoon the lentils into a bowl. Fry the egg in the same skillet over medium heat with the lid on, 3 to 4 minutes, until the white is set and the yolk is firm (160F).\n7. Top the lentils with the egg and the Greek yogurt, then add a big squeeze of lemon and a handful of chopped parsley.",
