 "method": "1. Rub the tofu cubes with the spices and roast at 425F for 20 minutes until the edges char. 2. Soften the onion and garlic in the oil, add the spices, then the tomato, and simmer 12 minutes. 3. Blend the sauce smooth. 4. Stir in the tofu and spinach.",
 "batchQ": 3, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a sheet pan, parchment, a large pot, a stick blender, a small pot for the grain, a cutting board, a knife and 5 containers.\n2. Press the tofu in a clean towel under something heavy for 15 minutes, because dry tofu roasts crisp and wet tofu steams.\n3. Heat the oven to 425F. Cut the tofu into 1-inch cubes and toss them with half of your fat, 1 tsp garam masala, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp turmeric and 1/2 tsp salt. Roast them on the lined sheet pan in a single layer 20 to 25 minutes, turning once, until browned and charred at the edges; that char is the tikka flavour.\n4. Cook your grain while the tofu roasts: rinse it, then simmer it covered in salted water until tender and the water is absorbed (white rice takes about 18 minutes in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup; brown rice 40 to 45 minutes in 2 cups per cup). Rest it 5 minutes off the heat, fluff it and spread it on a tray to cool. Weigh it cooked.\n5. Dice the onion, mince the garlic, grate 1 tbsp ginger and chop the tomato. If it is the bell pepper, dice it and cook it with the onion. If it is the spinach, keep it whole for the end.\n6. Heat the rest of your fat in the large pot over medium and cook the onion 6 to 8 minutes, until soft and golden, then add the garlic, the ginger, 2 tsp garam masala, 1 tsp cumin and 1/2 tsp turmeric and stir 1 minute, so the spices toast instead of tasting raw.\n7. Add the tomato with 1 cup of water and 1 tsp salt and simmer uncovered 12 to 15 minutes, until the tomato has collapsed and thickened.\n8. Blend the sauce smooth in the pot with the stick blender. Taste and add salt or a squeeze of lemon if it is flat.\n9. Stir the roasted tofu into the sauce. If it is the spinach, stir it in now until it wilts, about 1 minute.\n10. Ladle the curry into the 5 containers straight away with the cooled grain next to it; a full pot cools too slowly to be safe. Leave the lids off until the steam stops, 20 to 30 minutes, then seal, write the date on each, and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n11. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months.\n12. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes, stirring halfway, or warm it in a pan with a splash of water. Cilantro and lemon on top.",
 "makes": 5,
