 "method": "1. Slice the tempeh 1/4 inch thick, so it crisps all the way through.\n2. Heat a little oil in a nonstick pan over medium heat and fry the tempeh 3 to 4 minutes a side, until deep golden and crisp at the edges. For the last minute, add the soy sauce, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika and 1/2 tsp maple syrup and turn the slices until glazed.\n3. Toast the rye bread 2 to 3 minutes, until crisp, and spread it with the Dijon mustard.\n4. Layer the tempeh and the sauerkraut onto the rye bread, then add your vegetables. If your fat is the avocado, slice it and lay it over the tempeh.\n5. Close the sandwich. If your fat is the olive oil, brush it over the outside of the bread so it crisps. Press the sandwich in a hot pan over medium heat 1 minute a side, until the bread is crisp and the filling is hot, then serve.",
