 "method": "1. Cook the rice first, because it takes the longest. If your grain is the white rice, rinse it, simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice, 18 to 20 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked. If your grain is the brown rice, rinse it, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice, 40 to 45 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked.\n2. Press the tofu dry between towels and crumble it into small pieces, so it browns instead of steaming.\n3. Heat the avocado oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat. Add the tofu and fry 6 to 8 minutes, stirring now and then, until golden and a little crisp. Push it to the side.\n4. Add the garlic and 1/2 tsp chili flakes to the cleared side and cook 30 seconds, until fragrant, so the garlic does not burn.\n5. Add your vegetables and stir-fry 3 to 5 minutes, until crisp-tender, adding a splash of water and covering for the last minute if they are still firm.\n6. Stir in the soy sauce and 1/2 tsp honey and toss 1 minute. Take the pan off the heat and toss in a big handful of basil, so it wilts but keeps its aroma.\n7. Serve over your grain with a squeeze of lime.",
