 "method": "1. Rub the tofu slabs with the jerk seasoning and roast or grill until charred. 2. Simmer the rice and kidney beans with thyme and a little onion. 3. Steam the cabbage, carrot and pepper. 4. Serve together.",
 "batchQ": 2, "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a sheet pan, parchment, a medium pot with a lid, a steamer basket, a small bowl, a grater, paper towels, and 5 containers.\n2. Heat the oven to 425F and press the tofu between paper towels under a heavy pan for 15 minutes; a dry surface lets the rub stick and char.\n3. Make the jerk rub in the small bowl: half the onion (grated), the garlic (minced), 2 tsp allspice, 2 tsp dried thyme, 1/2 tsp cayenne, 2 tbsp soy sauce, the juice of 1 lime, 1 tbsp maple and half the avocado oil.\n4. Cut the tofu into slabs about 3/4 inch thick, coat them in the rub, and lay them on the lined pan with space between them.\n5. Roast the tofu 25 to 30 minutes, turning once, until the edges are dark and charred.\n6. Cook your carb while the tofu roasts: if it is the kidney beans, drain and rinse them and warm them in the pot with the rest of the onion, 1 tsp dried thyme and 1/2 cup water, 5 to 8 minutes, until hot through. If it is the rice, rinse it and simmer it covered with the rest of the onion and 1 tsp dried thyme in salted water until tender (white rice takes about 18 minutes in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup; brown rice 40 to 45 minutes in 2 cups per cup), then rest it 5 minutes, fluff it, and weigh it cooked.\n7. Slice your vegetables thin so they steam in the same time.\n8. Steam them in the basket over an inch of simmering water, 5 to 7 minutes, until just tender with some bite; they soften again every time you reheat.\n9. Cool everything uncovered until it stops steaming, 20 to 30 minutes, because trapped steam turns the tofu soft.\n10. Divide the tofu, your carb and your vegetables between the 5 containers, seal, write the date on each, and refrigerate within 1 hour; cooked grains cooled slowly are the classic food-poisoning risk.\n11. Keep the lime wedges separate for serving.\n12. Storage: fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months.\n13. Reheat: microwave 2 to 3 minutes with a splash of water, stirring halfway, until steaming hot, or crisp the tofu 4 to 5 minutes in an air fryer at 400F. Squeeze lime over the top.",
