 "method": "1. Cook the rice first, because it takes the longest. If your grain is the white rice, rinse it, simmer it covered in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup of rice, 18 to 20 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked. If your grain is the brown rice, rinse it, simmer it covered in 2 cups of water per cup of rice, 40 to 45 minutes, rest it 5 minutes off the heat and weigh it cooked.\n2. Slice the seitan thin. Heat your fat in a large skillet over high heat, add the seitan and sear it 4 to 5 minutes, turning now and then, until browned and crisp at the edges. Move it to a plate.\n3. Add 1/4 cup of water to the same pan. If your vegetables are the broccoli, cut it into small florets and steam it covered 3 to 4 minutes, until bright green and just tender. If your vegetables are the bok choy, chop it and steam it covered 2 to 3 minutes, until the stems are tender.\n4. Add the garlic and 1/2 tsp grated ginger and stir 30 seconds, until fragrant. Return the seitan with the soy sauce, 1 tsp rice vinegar and 1/2 tsp honey and let it bubble 1 to 2 minutes, until the sauce reduces and clings.\n5. Serve over your grain, topped with a sprinkle of sesame seeds.",
