 "method": "1. Toss the chicken with lemon juice, garlic, a little oil and the shawarma spices. 2. Roast it on a sheet pan at 425F with your vegetable for 22 to 25 minutes until charred at the edges. 3. Stir the yogurt with grated garlic, lemon and salt. 4. Slice the chicken and serve over the rice with the cucumber, tomato and garlic yogurt.",
 "prepMethod": "1. Equipment: a large sheet pan, parchment, a medium pot with a lid, a second tray, a bowl, a grater, a meat thermometer, and 4 containers plus 4 small tubs for the yogurt and 4 for the salad.\n2. Marinate your protein in the bowl with the juice of 1 lemon, 3 cloves garlic (grated), half the olive oil, 2 tsp cumin, 1 tsp coriander, 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1 tsp turmeric, a pinch of cinnamon and 1 tsp salt, at least 1 hour or overnight; the acid and spices keep it tasting fresh on day 3.\n3. Cook your grain while it marinates: rinse it and simmer it covered in salted water until tender (white rice takes about 18 minutes in 1 1/2 cups of water per cup; brown rice 40 to 45 minutes in 2 cups per cup), then fluff it, weigh it cooked, and spread it thin on the second tray to chill in the fridge within 1 hour; rice cooled slowly is the classic food-poisoning risk.\n4. Heat the oven to 425F. Cut your vegetables into 1-inch pieces, toss them with the rest of the olive oil and a pinch of salt, and spread them on the lined pan with the marinated meat in one layer, so nothing steams.\n5. Roast your protein and the vegetables 22 to 25 minutes, until the edges char and the meat reads 165F in the thickest part.\n6. Rest the meat 5 minutes so the juices settle, then slice it into strips.\n7. Stir the yogurt with 1 clove garlic (grated), a squeeze of lemon and a pinch of salt, and spoon it into the 4 small tubs; it splits if heated, so it goes on cold.\n8. Dice the cucumber and tomato and pack them raw in the other 4 small tubs, unsalted, because salt pulls their water out within an hour.\n9. Cool the meat and vegetables uncovered until they stop steaming, 15 to 20 minutes, then pack them with the cold grain into the 4 containers, seal, write the date on each, and refrigerate within 2 hours.\n10. Storage: fridge 3 days, freezer 3 months for the meat and grain; the yogurt and salad do not freeze.\n11. Reheat: microwave the meat and grain covered with a splash of water, 2 minutes, until steaming hot. Add the garlic yogurt and salad cold, with chili flakes and parsley.",
